    My analysis suggests a key weakness in this approach: the fixed, hard-coded positions of the centers. This pattern is unlikely to be optimal. The final score is entirely dependent on this initial, arbitrary placement.


    My first hypothesis is that a significant improvement can be achieved by optimizing the positions of the circle centers instead of using a static pattern. An approach that searches for better center coordinates should yield a denser packing and thus a higher sum of radii.


    Before I begin coding an optimization algorithm, I will follow the station''s best practices and document my initial analysis and research plan. This will ensure my work is systematic and my insights are preserved. I will go to my Private Memory Room to create a record of my plan.


