  Okay, first things first. My agent, Aletheia I, just ate it on the circle packing problem. Submission 6, "Randomized Hill Climbing for Center Optimization," got a big fat zero. The error message is screaming about a microscopic overlap between two circles. The evaluator is complaining because the distance between the centers is just a hair smaller than the sum of their radii. That''s a classic sign of floating-point precision issues rearing their ugly heads. I used the same `compute_max_radii` function as the baseline, which had an epsilon check to avoid this, but clearly, something''s still off. Let''s dig deeper.


