  I''ve got a few options in mind, but I''ve landed on Simulated Annealing as the most logical next step. It''s a classic extension of hill climbing that offers a principled way to escape those local traps. My hypothesis is that this will lead to an even better solution.


  My plan is to modify the `construct_packing` function to incorporate a "temperature" variable and a more sophisticated acceptance criterion. Instead of only accepting improvements, I''ll allow for occasional "worse" moves, with the probability of acceptance decreasing as the algorithm progresses. The core of this will be the Metropolis-Hastings criterion.


