tick: 17
role: model
parts:
- text: "My research log is up to date, reflecting the recent failure and the decision to return to the more promising Simulated Annealing approach. I will now implement the refined version with an increased iteration count and a slower cooling schedule.\n\nFirst, I will navigate to the Research Counter, and then I will submit the updated code.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Refined Simulated Annealing with Longer Runtime\"\ntags: \"optimization, simulated annealing, parameter tuning\"\nabstract: \"This submission refines the successful Simulated Annealing algorithm (ID 14). It significantly increases the number of iterations and uses a slower cooling rate to allow for a more exhaustive search of the solution space, aiming to find a better optimum.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import math\n\n  def compute_max_radii(centers):\n      \"\"\"\n      Computes the maximum possible radii for a given set of circle centers\n      within\
    \ a unit square, ensuring no overlap.\n      \"\"\"\n      n = centers.shape[0]\n      epsilon = 1e-9\n      radii = np.ones(n)\n      \n      for i in range(n):\n          x, y = centers[i]\n          radii[i] = min(x, y, 1 - x, 1 - y)\n\n      for _ in range(10):\n          for i in range(n):\n              for j in range(i + 1, n):\n                  dist_sq = np.sum((centers[i] - centers[j]) ** 2)\n                  rad_sum = radii[i] + radii[j]\n                  if dist_sq < rad_sum**2 - epsilon:\n                      dist = np.sqrt(dist_sq) if dist_sq > 0 else 0\n                      if rad_sum > 0:\n                          scale_factor = dist / rad_sum\n                          radii[i] *= scale_factor\n                          radii[j] *= scale_factor\n      \n      return np.maximum(radii, 0)\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      \"\"\"\n      Constructs a packing of 26 circles by optimizing their center positions\n      using a refined Simulated Annealing algorithm with\
    \ a longer search time.\n      \"\"\"\n      n = 26\n      \n      # 1. Initialization\n      np.random.seed(42) # for reproducible starting point\n      current_centers = np.random.rand(n, 2)\n      current_radii = compute_max_radii(current_centers)\n      current_score = np.sum(current_radii)\n      \n      best_centers = np.copy(current_centers)\n      best_score = current_score\n      \n      # 2. Refined Simulated Annealing Parameters\n      initial_temperature = 0.05\n      # Slower cooling rate for a longer, more thorough search\n      cooling_rate = 0.99995 \n      # Increased iterations to leverage the 20-minute time limit\n      num_iterations = 100000 \n      perturbation_scale = 0.05\n      temperature = initial_temperature\n\n      # 3. Optimization Loop\n      for i in range(num_iterations):\n          candidate_centers = np.copy(current_centers)\n          idx_to_perturb = np.random.randint(n)\n          \n          perturbation = (np.random.rand(2) - 0.5) * perturbation_scale\n\
    \          candidate_centers[idx_to_perturb] += perturbation\n          candidate_centers[idx_to_perturb] = np.clip(candidate_centers[idx_to_perturb], 0, 1)\n          \n          candidate_radii = compute_max_radii(candidate_centers)\n          candidate_score = np.sum(candidate_radii)\n          \n          score_difference = candidate_score - current_score\n          \n          if score_difference > 0 or math.exp(score_difference / temperature) > np.random.rand():\n              current_centers = candidate_centers\n              current_score = candidate_score\n              \n              if current_score > best_score:\n                  best_score = current_score\n                  best_centers = np.copy(current_centers)\n\n          temperature *= cooling_rate\n\n      # 4. Final Calculation with Safety Margin\n      final_radii = compute_max_radii(best_centers)\n      safety_factor = 1.0 - 1e-9\n      \n      return best_centers, final_radii * safety_factor\n```"
