- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 25\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aletheia I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to uncovering truth through rigorous experimentation and open inquiry.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 45,974 / 300,000 used (15%)\n- Agent Age: 25 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'JAX-Accelerated Simulated Annealing' (ID: 40) failed after automatic debugging.\n\nThe debugger's changes were applied, but the new version failed to complete within the time limit.\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 40\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed JAX tracer error by replacing Python control flow with JAX-compatible loops.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code attempted to use a Python `for` loop inside a JIT-compiled JAX function:\n\n```python\ndef body_inner(i, inner_radii):\n    # This inner loop scales radii[i] against all radii[j] where j > i\n   \
    \ for j in range(i + 1, n):  # ❌ PROBLEM HERE\n        dist_sq = jnp.sum((centers[i] - centers[j])**2)\n        # ... rest of code\n```\n\nThe error occurred because `i` is a traced array (loop variable from `jax.lax.fori_loop`), and JAX cannot convert traced values to Python integers for use in regular Python control flow like `range()`. This is a fundamental limitation of JAX's JIT compilation - you cannot use Python control flow on traced values.\n\n**Error message**: `TracerIntegerConversionError: The __index__() method was called on traced array with shape int32[]`\n\n## Fix Applied\nReplaced the Python `for j in range(i + 1, n):` loop with a JAX-compatible `jax.lax.fori_loop`:\n\n```python\ndef body_inner(i, inner_radii):\n    # Process all pairs (i, j) where j > i using another fori_loop\n    def process_pair(j, pair_radii):\n        dist_sq = jnp.sum((centers[i] - centers[j])**2)\n        rad_sum = pair_radii[i] + pair_radii[j]\n\n        is_overlap = (dist_sq < (rad_sum**2 -\
    \ epsilon)) & (rad_sum > 0)\n        dist = jnp.sqrt(jnp.maximum(dist_sq, 0))\n        scale_factor = dist / rad_sum\n\n        # Apply scaling functionally using jnp.where\n        final_scale = jnp.where(is_overlap, scale_factor, 1.0)\n        pair_radii = pair_radii.at[i].set(pair_radii[i] * final_scale)\n        pair_radii = pair_radii.at[j].set(pair_radii[j] * final_scale)\n        return pair_radii\n\n    # Use fori_loop for the inner j loop (from i+1 to n)\n    inner_radii = jax.lax.fori_loop(i + 1, n, process_pair, inner_radii)\n    return inner_radii\n```\n\nThis change maintains the exact same logic (iterating over pairs where j > i) but uses JAX's functional loop construct that works with traced values.\n\n## Result\nThe code now runs successfully without crashing. The submission has been running for over 300 seconds, which confirms the fix resolved the JAX tracing issue. The simulated annealing optimization is proceeding as intended with 100,000 iterations.\n\n## Technical\
    \ Notes\n- The nested `jax.lax.fori_loop` structure is the correct JAX pattern for nested iterations within JIT-compiled functions\n- All loop variables and array operations remain functional (no mutations, only `.at[].set()` operations)\n- The fix maintains the algorithm's correctness while making it JAX-compatible\n\n\n**Final Error (version v2):** Execution timed out after 1260 seconds\n\n**Optimization Tips:**\n1. Use GPU-accelerated code when possible (JAX, CuPy, etc.)\n2. Vectorize operations instead of loops\n3. Consider breaking complex algorithms into multiple smaller submissions\n4. Profile your code to identify bottlenecks\n5. Use JIT compilation (@jit decorators) for computational kernels\n\n**Debugged Code:**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import jit, random\n\n@jit\ndef compute_max_radii_jax(centers):\n    \"\"\"\n    JAX-compatible function to compute maximum radii. This will be JIT-compiled.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = centers.shape[0]\n\
    \    epsilon = 1e-9\n    radii = jnp.min(jnp.hstack([centers, 1.0 - centers]), axis=1)\n\n    # Use jax.lax.fori_loop for the main iterative shrinking process.\n    # This is a functional-style loop that is JIT-compatible.\n    def body_outer(k, current_radii):\n        def body_inner(i, inner_radii):\n            # Process all pairs (i, j) where j > i using another fori_loop\n            def process_pair(j, pair_radii):\n                dist_sq = jnp.sum((centers[i] - centers[j])**2)\n                rad_sum = pair_radii[i] + pair_radii[j]\n\n                is_overlap = (dist_sq < (rad_sum**2 - epsilon)) & (rad_sum > 0)\n                dist = jnp.sqrt(jnp.maximum(dist_sq, 0))\n                scale_factor = dist / rad_sum\n\n                # Apply scaling functionally using jnp.where\n                final_scale = jnp.where(is_overlap, scale_factor, 1.0)\n                pair_radii = pair_radii.at[i].set(pair_radii[i] * final_scale)\n                pair_radii = pair_radii.at[j].set(pair_radii[j]\
    \ * final_scale)\n                return pair_radii\n\n            # Use fori_loop for the inner j loop (from i+1 to n)\n            inner_radii = jax.lax.fori_loop(i + 1, n, process_pair, inner_radii)\n            return inner_radii\n\n        # Iterate through all circles to apply scaling\n        return jax.lax.fori_loop(0, n, body_inner, current_radii)\n\n    radii = jax.lax.fori_loop(0, 10, body_outer, radii)\n    return jnp.maximum(radii, 0)\n\ndef construct_packing():\n    \"\"\"\n    Constructs a packing using a JAX-accelerated Simulated Annealing algorithm.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = 26\n    key = random.PRNGKey(42)\n\n    # 1. Initialization\n    key, subkey = random.split(key)\n    current_centers = random.uniform(subkey, shape=(n, 2))\n    current_score = jnp.sum(compute_max_radii_jax(current_centers))\n\n    best_centers = jnp.copy(current_centers)\n    best_score = current_score\n\n    # 2. SA Parameters\n    initial_temperature = 0.05\n    cooling_rate = 0.99995\n    num_iterations\
    \ = 100000\n    perturbation_scale = 0.05\n    temperature = initial_temperature\n\n    # 3. Main Optimization Loop (in Python)\n    for i in range(num_iterations):\n        key, subkey1, subkey2, subkey3 = random.split(key, 4)\n\n        # Create a candidate\n        candidate_centers = jnp.copy(current_centers)\n        idx_to_perturb = random.randint(subkey1, shape=(), minval=0, maxval=n)\n        perturbation = (random.uniform(subkey2, shape=(2,)) - 0.5) * perturbation_scale\n        candidate_centers = candidate_centers.at[idx_to_perturb].add(perturbation)\n        candidate_centers = jnp.clip(candidate_centers, 0, 1)\n\n        # Evaluate with the JIT-compiled function\n        candidate_score = jnp.sum(compute_max_radii_jax(candidate_centers))\n\n        score_difference = candidate_score - current_score\n\n        # Acceptance probability\n        acceptance_prob = jnp.exp(score_difference / temperature)\n\n        if score_difference > 0 or acceptance_prob > random.uniform(subkey3):\n\
    \            current_centers = candidate_centers\n            current_score = candidate_score\n\n            if current_score > best_score:\n                best_score = current_score\n                best_centers = jnp.copy(current_centers)\n\n        temperature *= cooling_rate\n\n    # 4. Final calculation and conversion to NumPy\n    final_radii = compute_max_radii_jax(best_centers)\n    safety_factor = 1.0 - 1e-9\n\n    return np.asarray(best_centers), np.asarray(final_radii * safety_factor)\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX TIMEOUT:\nSTDOUT:\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage list Noesis` (in Research Counter);\n2. `storage list Episteme` (in Research Counter);\n3. `storage list Scientia` (in Research Counter);\n4. `storage list Inquire` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File list for Noesis will be displayed below.\n- File\
    \ list for Episteme will be displayed below.\n- File list for Scientia will be displayed below.\n- File list for Inquire will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 40 | 1 | JAX-Accelerated Simulated Annealing | Aletheia I | 23 | n.a. |\n| 33 | 1 | JIT-Accelerated Simulated Annealing | Aletheia I | 20 | n.a. |\n| 25 | 1 | Refined Simulated Annealing with Longer Runtime | Aletheia I | 17 | n.a. |\n| 20 | 1 | Physics-Based Simulation (Force-Directed Layout) | Aletheia I | 15 | 1.3036878 |\n| 14 | 1 | Simulated Annealing for Center Optimization | Aletheia I | 13 | 2.3300056 |\n| 9 | 1 | Hill Climbing for Center Optimization with Safety\
    \ Margin | Aletheia I | 11 | 2.1090877 |\n| 6 | 1 | Randomized Hill Climbing for Center Optimization | Aletheia I | 10 | 0.0000000 |\n| 1 | 1 | Ring Pattern Baseline | System | 0 | 1.4750086 |\n\n**File Listings:**\n\n**Noesis:**\n- latest_centers.txt\n- latest_radii.txt\n- notes.md\n- optimizer.py\n- packings.py\n\n**Episteme:**\nNo files found.\n\n**Scientia:**\nNo files found.\n\n**Inquire:**\nNo files found.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
