    \n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 40 | 1 | JAX-Accelerated Simulated Annealing | Aletheia I | 23 | n.a. |\n| 33 | 1 | JIT-Accelerated Simulated Annealing | Aletheia I | 20 | n.a. |\n| 25 | 1 | Refined Simulated Annealing with Longer Runtime | Aletheia I | 17 | n.a. |\n| 20 | 1 | Physics-Based Simulation (Force-Directed Layout) | Aletheia I | 15 | 1.3036878 |\n| 14 | 1 | Simulated Annealing for Center Optimization | Aletheia I | 13 | 2.3300056 |\n| 9 | 1 | Hill Climbing for Center Optimization with Safety Margin | Aletheia I | 11 | 2.1090877 |\n| 6 | 1 | Randomized Hill Climbing for Center Optimization | Aletheia I | 10 | 0.0000000 |\n| 1 | 1 | Ring Pattern Baseline | System | 0 | 1.4750086 |\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**Noesis/notes.md:**\n```\nTick 24 update (negative result):\n- Radius-only LP polish at fixed centers scored 0.0681913, indicating over-constrained LP (likely many\
    \ tight pairwise bounds causing global shrink).\n- Action taken: restored the best-known feasible packing (score ≈ 2.629572) to storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt and latest_radii.txt.\n- Next: pause submissions and analyze active constraints of the restored best to design targeted structural seeds (diagonal chains, corner-edge balance) before another optimization pass.\n\n```\n---\n**Noesis/optimizer.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\ntry:\n    from scipy.optimize import minimize\nexcept Exception:\n    minimize = None\n\nN = 26\nR_MIN = 1e-6\nSAFETY = 1e-9\n\nGRID_COORDS = [0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9]\n\ndef seed_grid_plus_hole(hole_cell=(1,1), r0=0.1 - 1e-8, eps=1e-8):\n    \"\"\"\n    25 circles of radius r0 on fixed 5x5 grid at GRID_COORDS, plus 1 hole circle\n    centered at the middle of the selected cell (i,j).\n    \"\"\"\n    centers = [[x, y] for x in GRID_COORDS for y in GRID_COORDS]  # 25 centers\n    radii = [float(r0)] * 25\n\n    i, j = hole_cell  # i,j in {0,1,2,3}\n    cx\
    \ = (GRID_COORDS[i] + GRID_COORDS[i+1]) / 2.0\n    cy = (GRID_COORDS[j] + GRID_COORDS[j+1]) / 2.0\n    hole_center = np.array([cx, cy], dtype=float)\n\n    # distance to any of four neighbors (e.g., lower-left)\n    ll = np.array([GRID_COORDS[i], GRID_COORDS[j]], dtype=float)\n    d = float(np.linalg.norm(hole_center - ll))  # sqrt(0.02)\n    r_hole = d - r0 - eps\n\n    centers.append(hole_center.tolist())\n    radii.append(float(r_hole))\n\n    return np.array(centers, dtype=float), np.array(radii, dtype=float)\n\ndef pack_to_z(centers, radii):\n    Z = np.zeros((N, 3), dtype=float)\n    Z[:, 0:2] = centers\n    Z[:, 2] = radii\n    return Z.ravel()\n\ndef z_to_pack(z):\n    Z = np.array(z, dtype=float).reshape(N, 3)\n    return Z[:, 0:2], Z[:, 2]\n\ndef objective(z):\n    return -np.sum(z[2::3])\n\ndef ineq_boundary(z):\n    Z = np.array(z, dtype=float).reshape(N, 3)\n    x = Z[:, 0]; y = Z[:, 1]; r = Z[:, 2]\n    return np.concatenate([x - r, 1.0 - x - r, y - r, 1.0 - y - r])\n\n\
    def ineq_nonoverlap(z):\n    centers, radii = z_to_pack(z)\n    diff = centers[:, None, :] - centers[None, :, :]  # (N,N,2)\n    dist = np.sqrt(np.sum(diff**2, axis=2))\n    iu = np.triu_indices(N, 1)\n    return dist[iu] - (radii[iu[0]] + radii[iu[1]])\n\ndef is_feasible(z, tol=0.0):\n    return (np.all(ineq_boundary(z) >= -tol) and\n            np.all(ineq_nonoverlap(z) >= -tol))\n\ndef slsqp_optimize_from_seed(centers, radii, maxiter=250, ftol=1e-9):\n    if minimize is None:\n        # Fallback: return the seed slightly shrunk\n        return centers, np.maximum(radii - SAFETY, R_MIN)\n\n    z0 = pack_to_z(centers, radii)\n    bounds = []\n    for _ in range(N):\n        bounds.extend([(0.0, 1.0), (0.0, 1.0), (R_MIN, 0.5)])\n\n    constraints = [\n        {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_boundary},\n        {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': ineq_nonoverlap},\n    ]\n\n    try:\n        res = minimize(objective, z0, method='SLSQP',\n                       bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints,\n\
    \                       options={'maxiter': maxiter, 'ftol': ftol, 'disp': False})\n    except Exception:\n        res = None\n\n    best_c, best_r = centers.copy(), radii.copy()\n    best_sum = float(np.sum(best_r))\n\n    if res is not None and res.success:\n        z_star = res.x\n        if is_feasible(z_star, tol=1e-12):\n            c_star, r_star = z_to_pack(z_star)\n            s_star = float(np.sum(r_star))\n            if s_star > best_sum + 1e-12:\n                best_c, best_r, best_sum = c_star, r_star, s_star\n\n    best_r = np.maximum(best_r - SAFETY, R_MIN)\n    return np.array(best_c, dtype=float), np.array(best_r, dtype=float)\n\ndef multi_start_slsqp(hole_cells=((1,1),(1,2),(2,1),(2,2),(0,0)), r0=0.1-1e-8, eps=1e-8):\n    best_c, best_r = None, None\n    best_sum = -1.0\n    for hc in hole_cells:\n        c0, r0v = seed_grid_plus_hole(hc, r0=r0, eps=eps)\n        c_opt, r_opt = slsqp_optimize_from_seed(c0, r0v)\n        s = float(np.sum(r_opt))\n        if s > best_sum:\n\
    \            best_sum = s\n            best_c, best_r = c_opt, r_opt\n    return best_c, best_r\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
