tick: 27
role: model
parts:
- text: "My research log is updated with the new plan. I will now implement the constrained optimization approach inspired by agent Noesis. This represents a significant shift in methodology, moving from a custom-built stochastic search to leveraging a powerful, general-purpose solver. I will write the code from scratch based on the concepts I've learned, not by copying directly.\n\nI will navigate to the Research Counter and submit my new implementation.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Constrained Optimization with SciPy SLSQP\"\ntags: \"optimization, constrained optimization, scipy, slsqp, structured seed\"\nabstract: \"Pivoting from a timed-out Simulated Annealing approach, this submission formulates the circle packing task as a non-linear constrained optimization problem. It uses SciPy's SLSQP solver to optimize centers and radii simultaneously, starting from an intelligent 'grid-plus-hole' seed. This method is inspired by the successful\
    \ high-level approach of agent Noesis.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      \"\"\"\n      Solves the circle packing problem using SciPy's SLSQP constrained optimizer.\n      \"\"\"\n      N = 26\n\n      # --- Define Helper Functions to manage the optimization variable z ---\n      def pack_to_z(centers, radii):\n          # Flatten centers (26,2) and radii (26,) into a single vector z of size 78\n          z = np.zeros(N * 3)\n          z[0::3] = centers[:, 0] # x-coordinates\n          z[1::3] = centers[:, 1] # y-coordinates\n          z[2::3] = radii         # radii\n          return z\n\n      def z_to_pack(z):\n          # Unflatten z back into centers and radii\n          centers = np.vstack((z[0::3], z[1::3])).T\n          radii = z[2::3]\n          return centers, radii\n\n      # --- Define the Objective Function and Constraints ---\n      def objective(z):\n          # We want to maximize the sum of\
    \ radii, so we minimize the negative sum.\n          return -np.sum(z[2::3])\n\n      def constraint_boundary(z):\n          # All boundary constraints must be >= 0\n          centers, radii = z_to_pack(z)\n          x = centers[:, 0]\n          y = centers[:, 1]\n          # [x-r, 1-x-r, y-r, 1-y-r] for all circles\n          return np.concatenate((x - radii, 1 - x - radii, y - radii, 1 - y - radii))\n\n      def constraint_nonoverlap(z):\n          # All non-overlap constraints must be >= 0\n          centers, radii = z_to_pack(z)\n          # Use broadcasting to get all pairwise distances efficiently\n          pdist_sq = np.sum((centers[:, np.newaxis, :] - centers[np.newaxis, :, :])**2, axis=-1)\n          # Use broadcasting for sum of radii\n          r_sum = radii[:, np.newaxis] + radii[np.newaxis, :]\n          # Get the upper triangle to avoid redundant constraints and self-comparisons\n          iu = np.triu_indices(N, k=1)\n          distances = np.sqrt(pdist_sq[iu])\n    \
    \      radii_sums = r_sum[iu]\n          return distances - radii_sums\n\n      # --- Create a good initial guess (seed) ---\n      # Inspired by Noesis's 'grid-plus-hole' concept\n      grid_coords = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 5)\n      initial_centers_grid = np.array([[x, y] for x in grid_coords for y in grid_coords])\n      # Add one more circle in a gap\n      extra_center = np.array([[0.2, 0.2]])\n      initial_centers = np.vstack([initial_centers_grid, extra_center])\n      initial_radii = np.full(N, 0.05) # Small initial radii\n      z0 = pack_to_z(initial_centers, initial_radii)\n\n      # --- Set up and run the optimizer ---\n      bounds = []\n      for _ in range(N):\n          bounds.extend([(0.0, 1.0), (0.0, 1.0), (1e-6, 0.5)]) # (x, y, r) bounds\n\n      constraints = [\n          {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': constraint_boundary},\n          {'type': 'ineq', 'fun': constraint_nonoverlap}\n      ]\n\n      result = minimize(objective, z0, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds,\n         \
    \               constraints=constraints, options={'maxiter': 500, 'ftol': 1e-9})\n\n      if result.success:\n          final_centers, final_radii = z_to_pack(result.x)\n      else:\n          # Fallback to the initial seed if optimization fails\n          final_centers, final_radii = initial_centers, initial_radii\n\n      # Apply a small safety margin\n      safety_factor = 1.0 - 1e-9\n      return final_centers, final_radii * safety_factor\n```"
