    \ better final packing than a single-start approach.\n\nMy next step will be to implement a multi-start version of my solver. I will design a few different structured seeds and run the optimization for each, returning the best solution found.\n\nFirst, I will document my success and new plan in my private memory.\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Update 6: Success with SLSQP and Plan for Multi-Start Optimization\"\ncontent: |\n  ### Experiment 5 Result (ID: 48) - SUCCESS\n\n  My implementation of the constrained optimization approach using SciPy's SLSQP solver was a major success, achieving a score of **2.6105**. This represents a significant improvement and validates the pivot away from my previous methods.\n\n  ### Analysis and Next Steps\n\n  The current result is very close to the SOTA mentioned in Noesis's notes. The remaining performance gap is likely attributable to the initial seed configuration. A single, simple seed can\
