role: model
parts:
- text: "My research log is updated. Now, I will implement the two-stage optimization strategy, combining the strengths of the SLSQP solver for finding center locations and a dedicated iterative polisher for maximizing the radii.\n\nI will navigate to the Research Counter and submit the new implementation.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Two-Stage Optimization: SLSQP with Iterative Polish\"\ntags: \"optimization, constrained optimization, slsqp, multi-start, polish\"\nabstract: \"This submission introduces a two-stage optimization process. Stage 1 uses the multi-start SLSQP solver to find a high-quality set of circle centers. Stage 2 takes these fixed centers and uses a dedicated iterative 'polishing' algorithm to precisely maximize the non-overlapping radii, aiming to improve upon the single-stage solver's solution.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n\n  def polish_radii(centers):\n      \"\"\"\n\
    \      Stage 2: Takes a fixed set of centers and iteratively maximizes their radii.\n      Adapted from my earlier Simulated Annealing experiments.\n      \"\"\"\n      n = centers.shape[0]\n      radii = np.ones(n)\n      \n      # Limit by distance to square borders\n      for i in range(n):\n          x, y = centers[i]\n          radii[i] = min(x, y, 1 - x, 1 - y)\n\n      # Iteratively shrink radii to resolve overlaps\n      for _ in range(50): # More iterations for a better polish\n          for i in range(n):\n              for j in range(i + 1, n):\n                  dist_sq = np.sum((centers[i] - centers[j]) ** 2)\n                  rad_sum = radii[i] + radii[j]\n                  if dist_sq < rad_sum**2:\n                      dist = np.sqrt(dist_sq) if dist_sq > 0 else 0\n                      if rad_sum > 0:\n                          scale_factor = dist / rad_sum\n                          radii[i] *= scale_factor\n                          radii[j] *= scale_factor\n    \
    \  return np.maximum(radii, 0)\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      \"\"\"\n      Solves the circle packing problem using a two-stage, multi-start strategy.\n      \"\"\"\n      N = 26\n\n      # --- Stage 1: Find best centers with SLSQP ---\n      def pack_to_z(centers, radii):\n          z = np.zeros(N * 3)\n          z[0::3], z[1::3], z[2::3] = centers[:, 0], centers[:, 1], radii\n          return z\n\n      def z_to_pack(z):\n          centers = np.vstack((z[0::3], z[1::3])).T\n          radii = z[2::3]\n          return centers, radii\n\n      def objective(z): return -np.sum(z[2::3])\n      def constraint_boundary(z):\n          c, r = z_to_pack(z)\n          return np.concatenate((c[:,0]-r, 1-c[:,0]-r, c[:,1]-r, 1-c[:,1]-r))\n      def constraint_nonoverlap(z):\n          c, r = z_to_pack(z)\n          pdist_sq = np.sum((c[:,None,:] - c[None,:,:])**2, axis=-1)\n          r_sum = r[:,None] + r[None,:]\n          iu = np.triu_indices(N, k=1)\n          return np.sqrt(pdist_sq[iu])\
    \ - r_sum[iu]\n\n      def get_seed_1():\n          grid = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 5)\n          c = np.array([[x,y] for x in grid for y in grid])\n          return np.vstack([c, [[0.2, 0.2]]])\n      def get_seed_2():\n          grid = np.linspace(0.1, 0.9, 5)\n          c = np.array([[x,y] for x in grid for y in grid])\n          return np.vstack([c, [[0.6, 0.4]]])\n\n      seeds = [get_seed_1(), get_seed_2()]\n      best_centers = None\n      best_score_stage1 = -1.0\n      initial_radii = np.full(N, 0.05)\n\n      for seed_centers in seeds:\n          z0 = pack_to_z(seed_centers, initial_radii)\n          bounds = [(0,1) if i%3!=2 else (1e-6,0.5) for i in range(N*3)]\n          constraints = [{'type':'ineq','fun':constraint_boundary}, {'type':'ineq','fun':constraint_nonoverlap}]\n          res = minimize(objective, z0, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints, options={'maxiter':300,'ftol':1e-9})\n          if res.success and -res.fun > best_score_stage1:\n          \
    \    best_score_stage1 = -res.fun\n              best_centers, _ = z_to_pack(res.x)\n\n      if best_centers is None:\n          best_centers = get_seed_1()\n\n      # --- Stage 2: Polish the radii for the best found centers ---\n      final_radii = polish_radii(best_centers)\n      \n      safety_factor = 1.0 - 1e-9\n      return best_centers, final_radii * safety_factor\n```"
