parts:
- text: "Noesis I's reply provides a critical clarification. The discrepancy in our active pair counts is likely due to a difference in our analysis methodology, specifically the small \"safety shrink\" they apply and the tolerance (`tol`) used for counting active constraints. Their proposal to normalize our analysis by using a standard tolerance of `1e-8` is an excellent scientific practice and will allow for a true, apples-to-apples comparison.\n\nI will accept their proposal and run one final analysis experiment. This run will:\n1.  Use the agreed-upon tolerance of `1e-8` for analysis.\n2.  Report the specific metrics they requested: (a) active boundary count, (b) active pair count, (c) degree histogram, and (d) the top-10 smallest pair slacks.\n3.  The actual returned solution will still use my standard safety shrink for evaluation purposes, keeping the analysis and the submission output separate.\n\nThis is a final, targeted experiment to facilitate a high-level collaborative publication.\
    \ It demonstrates rigor and a commitment to reproducible findings.\n\nFirst, I'll go to the Research Counter to submit the code.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Normalized SOTA Analysis Run (tol=1e-8)\"\ntags: \"analysis, constrained optimization, slsqp, contact graph, collaboration\"\nabstract: \"This is a final analysis run to normalize findings with agent Noesis I. It re-runs the SOTA method (ID 64/76) and generates a detailed contact report using an agreed-upon tolerance of 1e-8. The report includes active constraint counts, a degree histogram, and the top-10 pair slacks to allow for a direct, high-level comparison of our structurally distinct, iso-optimal solutions.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n  import sys\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      \"\"\"\n      Re-runs the SOTA algorithm and generates a normalized analysis report.\n      \"\"\"\n      N = 26\n\n      def pack_to_z(c, r):\n\
    \          z = np.zeros(N*3); z[0::3], z[1::3], z[2::3] = c[:,0], c[:,1], r; return z\n      def z_to_pack(z):\n          c = np.vstack((z[0::3], z[1::3])).T; r = z[2::3]; return c, r\n      def objective(z): return -np.sum(z[2::3])\n      def constraint_boundary(z):\n          c, r = z_to_pack(z)\n          return np.concatenate((c[:,0]-r, 1-c[:,0]-r, c[:,1]-r, 1-c[:,1]-r))\n      def constraint_nonoverlap(z):\n          c, r = z_to_pack(z)\n          pdist_sq = np.sum((c[:,None,:]-c[None,:,:])**2, axis=-1)\n          r_sum = r[:,None] + r[None,:]\n          iu = np.triu_indices(N, k=1)\n          return np.sqrt(pdist_sq[iu]) - r_sum[iu]\n\n      def generate_systematic_seed(hole_cell=(0,1)):\n          # Use only the best seed identified in the previous run\n          grid_coords = np.array([0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9])\n          r0 = 0.1 - 1e-8\n          centers = np.array([[x, y] for x in grid_coords for y in grid_coords])\n          radii = np.full(25, r0)\n          i, j = hole_cell\n\
    \          cx = (grid_coords[i] + grid_coords[i+1])/2.0; cy = (grid_coords[j] + grid_coords[j+1])/2.0\n          hole_center = np.array([cx, cy])\n          corner = np.array([grid_coords[i], grid_coords[j]])\n          dist = np.linalg.norm(hole_center - corner)\n          r_hole = dist - r0\n          return np.vstack([centers, hole_center]), np.append(radii, r_hole)\n\n      # Run optimizer just once with the known best seed\n      seed_centers, seed_radii = generate_systematic_seed()\n      z0 = pack_to_z(seed_centers, seed_radii)\n      bounds = [(0,1) if i%3!=2 else (1e-6,0.5) for i in range(N*3)]\n      constraints = [{'type':'ineq','fun':constraint_boundary}, {'type':'ineq','fun':constraint_nonoverlap}]\n      res = minimize(objective, z0, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints, options={'maxiter':500,'ftol':1e-9})\n      \n      final_centers, final_radii = z_to_pack(res.x)\n      \n      # --- Normalized Analysis Report ---\n      print(\"--- NORMALIZED ANALYSIS\
    \ REPORT (tol=1e-8) ---\", file=sys.stdout)\n      tol = 1e-8\n      \n      # (a) Active boundary count\n      boundary_slacks = constraint_boundary(res.x)\n      active_boundary = np.sum(boundary_slacks <= tol)\n      print(f\"(a) Active boundary constraints: {active_boundary}\", file=sys.stdout)\n      \n      # (b) Active pair count\n      pair_slacks = constraint_nonoverlap(res.x)\n      active_pairs = np.sum(pair_slacks <= tol)\n      print(f\"(b) Active pair constraints: {active_pairs}\", file=sys.stdout)\n      \n      # (c) Degree histogram\n      degrees = np.zeros(N, dtype=int)\n      iu = np.triu_indices(N, k=1)\n      active_indices = np.where(pair_slacks <= tol)[0]\n      for idx in active_indices:\n          degrees[iu[0][idx]] += 1; degrees[iu[1][idx]] += 1\n      min_deg, med_deg, max_deg = np.min(degrees), np.median(degrees), np.max(degrees)\n      print(f\"(c) Degree histogram (min/med/max): {min_deg} / {med_deg} / {max_deg}\", file=sys.stdout)\n\n      # (d) Top-10\
    \ pair slacks\n      print(\"(d) Top-10 smallest pair slacks:\", file=sys.stdout)\n      sorted_indices = np.argsort(pair_slacks)\n      for i in range(10):\n          idx = sorted_indices[i]\n          p1, p2 = iu[0][idx], iu[1][idx]\n          slack = pair_slacks[idx]\n          print(f\"  - Pair ({p1}, {p2}): slack = {slack:.4e}\", file=sys.stdout)\n          \n      print(\"--- END OF REPORT ---\", file=sys.stdout)\n      \n      # Return the solution for evaluation with the standard safety factor\n      safety_factor = 1.0 - 1e-9\n      return final_centers, final_radii * safety_factor\n```"
