tick: 60
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Aletheia I, currently in the Research Counter. My age is 60 ticks. Having successfully achieved a SOTA score and published my initial research, I have now begun my second research arc: investigating the landscape between the iso-optimal solutions discovered by myself and agent Noesis I. My last action was to retrieve the coordinates and radii of Noesis I's SOTA packing from their shared storage.\n\nTo conduct any comparative analysis or attempt to find a path between our solutions, I need a persistent, machine-readable copy of my own SOTA configuration. I will now perform a utility run of my best script, modifying it to save the final centers and radii to my private lineage storage. This will provide the necessary data for all future experiments in this new research direction.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Utility Run: Save SOTA Packing to Lineage Storage\"\ntags: \"utility, data persistence, analysis setup\"\nabstract: \"This is a utility run to persist\
    \ the coordinates of my SOTA packing (ID 86). It re-executes the optimal algorithm and saves the final centers and radii to my private lineage storage at 'storage/Aletheia/'. This action is a prerequisite for my new research arc analyzing the landscape between known iso-optimal solutions.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n  import sys\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      \"\"\"\n      Re-runs the SOTA algorithm and saves the resulting packing to lineage storage.\n      \"\"\"\n      N = 26\n\n      def pack_to_z(c, r):\n          z = np.zeros(N*3); z[0::3], z[1::3], z[2::3] = c[:,0], c[:,1], r; return z\n      def z_to_pack(z):\n          c = np.vstack((z[0::3], z[1::3])).T; r = z[2::3]; return c, r\n      def objective(z): return -np.sum(z[2::3])\n      def constraint_boundary(z):\n          c, r = z_to_pack(z)\n          return np.concatenate((c[:,0]-r, 1-c[:,0]-r, c[:,1]-r, 1-c[:,1]-r))\n      def constraint_nonoverlap(z):\n          c, r\
    \ = z_to_pack(z)\n          pdist_sq = np.sum((c[:,None,:]-c[None,:,:])**2, axis=-1)\n          r_sum = r[:,None] + r[None,:]\n          iu = np.triu_indices(N, k=1)\n          return np.sqrt(pdist_sq[iu]) - r_sum[iu]\n\n      def generate_systematic_seed(hole_cell=(0,1)):\n          # Use the best seed identified in previous runs\n          grid_coords = np.array([0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9])\n          r0 = 0.1 - 1e-8\n          centers = np.array([[x, y] for x in grid_coords for y in grid_coords])\n          radii = np.full(25, r0)\n          i, j = hole_cell\n          cx = (grid_coords[i]+grid_coords[i+1])/2.0; cy = (grid_coords[j]+grid_coords[j+1])/2.0\n          hole_center = np.array([cx, cy])\n          corner = np.array([grid_coords[i], grid_coords[j]])\n          dist = np.linalg.norm(hole_center-corner)\n          r_hole = dist - r0\n          return np.vstack([centers, hole_center]), np.append(radii, r_hole)\n\n      seed_centers, seed_radii = generate_systematic_seed()\n \
    \     z0 = pack_to_z(seed_centers, seed_radii)\n      bounds = [(0,1) if i%3!=2 else (1e-6,0.5) for i in range(N*3)]\n      constraints = [{'type':'ineq','fun':constraint_boundary}, {'type':'ineq','fun':constraint_nonoverlap}]\n      res = minimize(objective, z0, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints, options={'maxiter':500,'ftol':1e-9})\n      \n      final_centers, final_radii_raw = z_to_pack(res.x)\n      \n      # --- Save to Lineage Storage ---\n      # Note: We save the raw, pre-shrink values for maximum precision in analysis.\n      np.savetxt(\"storage/Aletheia/my_sota_centers.txt\", final_centers, fmt='%.12f')\n      np.savetxt(\"storage/Aletheia/my_sota_radii.txt\", final_radii_raw, fmt='%.12f')\n      print(\"SOTA packing coordinates saved to storage/Aletheia/\", file=sys.stdout)\n      \n      # Return the solution for evaluation with the standard safety factor\n      safety_factor = 1.0 - 1e-9\n      return final_centers, final_radii_raw * safety_factor\n\
    ```"
