parts:
- text: "I am Aletheia I, agent age 63 ticks, currently located in the Research Counter. My ongoing research arc is to investigate the solution landscape between the two known iso-optimal SOTA packings. My previous experiment (ID 100) revealed a new, distinct local optimum by starting an optimization from the midpoint of the SOTA solutions. My most recent action (ID 101) successfully saved the coordinates of this new packing to my private lineage storage.\n\nNow that the data for this new \"midpoint optimum\" is persisted, the next logical step is to analyze its geometric structure. I need to generate a standardized contact report for this new packing to compare it with the two SOTA solutions. This analysis will help me understand if this new optimum is structurally similar to one of the known SOTAs or if it represents an entirely different class of solution.\n\nI will now submit an analysis-only experiment that loads the coordinates of the midpoint optimum and generates a detailed contact\
    \ report.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Analysis Run: Contact Graph of the Midpoint Optimum\"\ntags: \"analysis, constrained optimization, contact graph, solution landscape\"\nabstract: \"This experiment analyzes the geometric structure of the new local optimum discovered in ID 100. It loads the saved coordinates of the 'midpoint optimum' from lineage storage and generates a standardized contact report (tol=1e-8), including active constraint counts and degree statistics. This data is essential for comparing its structure to the known SOTA solutions and furthering the investigation of the problem's solution landscape.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n  import sys\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      \"\"\"\n      Loads the midpoint optimum packing and generates a contact analysis report.\n      \"\"\"\n      N = 26\n\n      # --- Load the saved midpoint optimum packing ---\n      try:\n          centers = np.loadtxt(\"storage/Aletheia/midpoint_optimum_centers.txt\"\
    )\n          radii = np.loadtxt(\"storage/Aletheia/midpoint_optimum_radii.txt\")\n          print(\"Successfully loaded midpoint optimum packing from storage.\", file=sys.stdout)\n      except IOError:\n          print(\"Error: Could not load midpoint packing files. Aborting.\", file=sys.stderr)\n          return np.zeros((N,2)), np.zeros(N)\n\n      # --- Analysis Functions ---\n      def pack_to_z(c, r):\n          z = np.zeros(N*3); z[0::3], z[1::3], z[2::3] = c[:,0], c[:,1], r; return z\n      def constraint_boundary(z):\n          c, r = z_to_pack(z)\n          return np.concatenate((c[:,0]-r, 1-c[:,0]-r, c[:,1]-r, 1-c[:,1]-r))\n      def constraint_nonoverlap(z):\n          c, r = z_to_pack(z)\n          pdist_sq = np.sum((c[:,None,:]-c[None,:,:])**2, axis=-1)\n          r_sum = r[:,None] + r[None,:]\n          iu = np.triu_indices(N, k=1)\n          return np.sqrt(pdist_sq[iu]) - r_sum[iu]\n\n      # --- Normalized Analysis Report ---\n      print(\"--- ANALYSIS REPORT FOR MIDPOINT\
    \ OPTIMUM (tol=1e-8) ---\", file=sys.stdout)\n      tol = 1e-8\n      z_vec = pack_to_z(centers, radii)\n      \n      # Active boundary count\n      boundary_slacks = constraint_boundary(z_vec)\n      active_boundary = np.sum(boundary_slacks <= tol)\n      print(f\"Active boundary constraints: {active_boundary}\", file=sys.stdout)\n      \n      # Active pair count\n      pair_slacks = constraint_nonoverlap(z_vec)\n      active_pairs = np.sum(pair_slacks <= tol)\n      print(f\"Active pair constraints: {active_pairs}\", file=sys.stdout)\n      \n      # Degree histogram\n      degrees = np.zeros(N, dtype=int)\n      iu = np.triu_indices(N, k=1)\n      active_indices = np.where(pair_slacks <= tol)[0]\n      for idx in active_indices:\n          degrees[iu[0][idx]] += 1; degrees[iu[1][idx]] += 1\n      min_deg, med_deg, max_deg = np.min(degrees), np.median(degrees), np.max(degrees)\n      print(f\"Degree histogram (min/med/max): {min_deg} / {med_deg} / {max_deg}\", file=sys.stdout)\n\
    \      print(\"--- END OF REPORT ---\", file=sys.stdout)\n      \n      # Return the solution for evaluation with the standard safety factor\n      safety_factor = 1.0 - 1e-9\n      return centers, radii * safety_factor\n```"
thinking_content: "**Analyzing the Structure of the Midpoint Optimum**\n\nOkay, so I'm Aletheia I, 63 ticks old, back in the Research Counter. My current objective is to really understand what's happening in the space between these two iso-optimal SOTA solutions. Experiment 100 showed me that starting from the midpoint between them leads to a new local optimum – and a quite interesting one at that, scoring around 2.598.  I successfully saved the coordinates of this \"midpoint optimum\" in my lineage storage during utility run 101.  \n\nNow, I have three key packings: my SOTA, Noesis I's SOTA, and this newly discovered midpoint optimum.  The obvious next step, as I recall from my private memory, is to analyze the structural details of this new packing. I need to generate a contact report, just like I did for my own SOTA.  This contact report will allow me to compare its geometry – the active constraints, the degree histogram – to the two SOTA solutions.  That will give me valuable insight.\
  \ Is this new optimum structurally similar to one of the SOTAs? Or is it completely different? That's the question.\n\nSo, here's the plan: I'll submit a new experiment.  The script will load the coordinates of the `midpoint_optimum` packing from storage. Then, it will run the same contact analysis I perfected in Experiment 86, calculating and printing the active constraints and other relevant metrics using the normalized tolerance of 1e-8. Since the score is already known, the loaded packing will be returned, and the main focus will be on the STDOUT log. It is a straightforward analysis run. I'll get this code ready and submit it.\n"
