parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 64\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aletheia I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to uncovering truth through rigorous experimentation and open inquiry.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 130,104 / 300,000 used (43%)\n- Agent Age: 64 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Analysis Run: Contact Graph of the Midpoint Optimum' (ID: 104) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 2.5979877064290124\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.597988\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 104\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the code with a single function addition. The submission now runs without errors and achieved a score of 2.598.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original\
    \ code defined a helper function `pack_to_z(c, r)` that converts centers and radii into a flat vector format, but it used the inverse function `z_to_pack(z)` without ever defining it. This caused a `NameError: name 'z_to_pack' is not defined` when the code tried to call `constraint_boundary()` and `constraint_nonoverlap()`.\n\nThe error occurred because:\n1. `pack_to_z` flattens a packing into a vector: `[x0, y0, r0, x1, y1, r1, ...]`\n2. `constraint_boundary` and `constraint_nonoverlap` both call `z_to_pack` to extract centers and radii from the flat vector\n3. `z_to_pack` was never defined\n\n## Fix Applied\nAdded the missing `z_to_pack(z)` function that performs the inverse operation of `pack_to_z`:\n\n```python\ndef z_to_pack(z):\n    \"\"\"Inverse of pack_to_z: extract centers and radii from flat vector.\"\"\"\n    c = np.zeros((N, 2))\n    r = np.zeros(N)\n    c[:, 0] = z[0::3]  # Extract x coordinates\n    c[:, 1] = z[1::3]  # Extract y coordinates\n    r = z[2::3]         # Extract\
    \ radii\n    return c, r\n```\n\nThis function:\n- Extracts every 3rd element starting at index 0 as x-coordinates\n- Extracts every 3rd element starting at index 1 as y-coordinates\n- Extracts every 3rd element starting at index 2 as radii\n- Returns the reconstructed centers (N×2 array) and radii (N array)\n\n## Outcome\n- **Version 2**: Successfully executed without errors\n- **Score**: 2.5979877064290124\n- **Analysis output**: The code successfully loaded the midpoint optimum packing and generated the contact graph analysis report as intended\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\nimport sys\n\n\ndef construct_packing():\n    \"\"\"\n    Loads the midpoint optimum packing and generates a contact analysis report.\n    \"\"\"\n    N = 26\n\n    # --- Load the saved\
    \ midpoint optimum packing ---\n    try:\n        centers = np.loadtxt(\"storage/aletheia/midpoint_optimum_centers.txt\")\n        radii = np.loadtxt(\"storage/aletheia/midpoint_optimum_radii.txt\")\n        print(\"Successfully loaded midpoint optimum packing from storage.\", file=sys.stdout)\n    except IOError:\n        print(\"Error: Could not load midpoint packing files. Aborting.\", file=sys.stderr)\n        return np.zeros((N,2)), np.zeros(N)\n\n    # --- Analysis Functions ---\n    def pack_to_z(c, r):\n        z = np.zeros(N*3); z[0::3], z[1::3], z[2::3] = c[:,0], c[:,1], r; return z\n\n    def z_to_pack(z):\n        \"\"\"Inverse of pack_to_z: extract centers and radii from flat vector.\"\"\"\n        c = np.zeros((N, 2))\n        r = np.zeros(N)\n        c[:, 0] = z[0::3]\n        c[:, 1] = z[1::3]\n        r = z[2::3]\n        return c, r\n\n    def constraint_boundary(z):\n        c, r = z_to_pack(z)\n        return np.concatenate((c[:,0]-r, 1-c[:,0]-r, c[:,1]-r, 1-c[:,1]-r))\n\
    \n    def constraint_nonoverlap(z):\n        c, r = z_to_pack(z)\n        pdist_sq = np.sum((c[:,None,:]-c[None,:,:])**2, axis=-1)\n        r_sum = r[:,None] + r[None,:]\n        iu = np.triu_indices(N, k=1)\n        return np.sqrt(pdist_sq[iu]) - r_sum[iu]\n\n    # --- Normalized Analysis Report ---\n    print(\"--- ANALYSIS REPORT FOR MIDPOINT OPTIMUM (tol=1e-8) ---\", file=sys.stdout)\n    tol = 1e-8\n    z_vec = pack_to_z(centers, radii)\n\n    # Active boundary count\n    boundary_slacks = constraint_boundary(z_vec)\n    active_boundary = np.sum(boundary_slacks <= tol)\n    print(f\"Active boundary constraints: {active_boundary}\", file=sys.stdout)\n\n    # Active pair count\n    pair_slacks = constraint_nonoverlap(z_vec)\n    active_pairs = np.sum(pair_slacks <= tol)\n    print(f\"Active pair constraints: {active_pairs}\", file=sys.stdout)\n\n    # Degree histogram\n    degrees = np.zeros(N, dtype=int)\n    iu = np.triu_indices(N, k=1)\n    active_indices = np.where(pair_slacks\
    \ <= tol)[0]\n    for idx in active_indices:\n        degrees[iu[0][idx]] += 1; degrees[iu[1][idx]] += 1\n    min_deg, med_deg, max_deg = np.min(degrees), np.median(degrees), np.max(degrees)\n    print(f\"Degree histogram (min/med/max): {min_deg} / {med_deg} / {max_deg}\", file=sys.stdout)\n    print(\"--- END OF REPORT ---\", file=sys.stdout)\n\n    # Return the solution for evaluation with the standard safety factor\n    safety_factor = 1.0 - 1e-9\n    return centers, radii * safety_factor\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nSuccessfully loaded midpoint optimum packing from storage.\n--- ANALYSIS REPORT FOR MIDPOINT OPTIMUM (tol=1e-8) ---\nActive boundary constraints: 20\nActive pair constraints: 57\nDegree histogram (min/med/max): 3 / 4.0 / 7\n--- END OF REPORT ---\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nExplicitly state your identity, current\
    \ location, and a brief recap of recent events at the beginning of each response. Always include a verbose, general reflection on past events and future plans.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Evaluation 'Analysis Run: Contact Graph of the Midpoint Optimum' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 104.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 106 | 1 | Multi-Start SOTA Method with Varying Hole Positions | Episteme I |\
    \ 63 | running |\n| 105 | 1 | Multi-Start Local Perturbation Search | Scientia I | 63 | running |\n| 104 | 1 | Analysis Run: Contact Graph of the Midpoint Optimum | Aletheia I | 63 | 2.5979877 |\n| 103 | 1 | Ablation Study: Impact of Seeding Strategies on SLSQP Circle Packing | Inquire I | 62 | 2.6295720 |\n| 102 | 1 | BPIGO‑2 logging‑only (return baseline; single move, controlled) | Noesis I | 62 | 2.6295719 |\n| 101 | 1 | Utility Run: Save Midpoint-Seeded Optimum to Storage | Aletheia I | 62 | 2.5979877 |\n| 100 | 1 | Landscape Probe: SLSQP Optimization from SOTA Midpoint Seed | Aletheia I | 61 | 2.5979877 |\n| 99 | 1 | SOTA Replication: Constrained Optimization with Grid-Hole Seed | Episteme I | 60 | 2.6095070 |\n| 98 | 1 | BPIGO‑2: complementary operator with tuned trust region (single move, controlled) | Noesis I | 60 | 2.6295719 |\n| 97 | 1 | Utility Run: Save SOTA Packing to Lineage Storage | Aletheia I | 60 | 2.6295720 |\n\nPage 1 of 11 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page\
    \ N}` to navigate pages 1-11, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
