parts:
- text: "I am Aletheia I, age 66, in the Research Counter. My analysis of the 25% interpolated seed experiment (ID 110) is complete, and the results are conclusive.\n\nThe analysis shows the resulting packing has **20** active boundary constraints and **58** active pair constraints. This contact graph is identical to my original SOTA solution. This confirms that the 25% interpolated seed lies within the basin of attraction of my SOTA packing. This is a very strong piece of evidence for my landscape mapping project.\n\nMy systematic probing is yielding clear results. The 50% point led to a new local optimum, while the 25% point was captured by my SOTA's basin of attraction. The logical continuation of this research is to probe the other side of the landscape. My next experiment will test the 75% interpolation point (i.e., 25% of the way from *my* SOTA towards Noesis I's). This will test the extent of the basin of attraction for Noesis I's solution and help complete the \"cross-section\" of\
    \ the landscape between our two optima.\n\nFirst, I will document my findings and the next step in my research log, then I will submit the experiment.\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Landscape Probe 3 Plan: Interpolation at 75%\"\ncontent: |\n  ### 25% Interpolation Analysis (ID: 110) - Results\n\n  The contact graph analysis of the SOTA solution found from the 25% interpolated seed is complete. The result has 20 active boundary and 58 active pair constraints.\n\n  ### Analysis\n  This contact graph is identical to that of my original SOTA solution. This provides strong evidence that the 25% interpolation point lies within the basin of attraction of my specific optimal packing.\n\n  ### Next Steps\n  To complete the picture, I will now probe the landscape from the other direction.\n\n  **Hypothesis for Experiment 3:** An SLSQP optimization started from a point 75% of the way between Noesis I's SOTA and my SOTA will likely converge\
    \ to Noesis I's SOTA solution, demonstrating the extent of its own basin of attraction.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Landscape Probe: SLSQP from 75% Interpolation Seed\"\ntags: \"analysis, constrained optimization, slsqp, solution landscape, interpolation\"\nabstract: \"This experiment continues the systematic mapping of the iso-optimal solution landscape. It seeds the SLSQP optimizer from a point interpolated 75% of the way from Noesis I's SOTA solution towards my own (i.e., closer to mine). The goal is to see if this point is still captured by the basin of attraction of my SOTA, or if it crosses over into Noesis I's basin or finds yet another feature.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n  import sys\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      \"\"\"\n      Initializes the SLSQP solver from a seed 75% of the way between two SOTA solutions.\n      \"\"\"\n      N = 26\n\n      def pack_to_z(c,\
    \ r):\n          z = np.zeros(N*3); z[0::3], z[1::3], z[2::3] = c[:,0], c[:,1], r; return z\n      def z_to_pack(z):\n          c = np.vstack((z[0::3], z[1::3])).T; r = z[2::3]; return c, r\n      def objective(z): return -np.sum(z[2::3])\n      def constraint_boundary(z):\n          c, r = z_to_pack(z)\n          return np.concatenate((c[:,0]-r, 1-c[:,0]-r, c[:,1]-r, 1-c[:,1]-r))\n      def constraint_nonoverlap(z):\n          c, r = z_to_pack(z)\n          pdist_sq = np.sum((c[:,None,:]-c[None,:,:])**2, axis=-1)\n          r_sum = r[:,None] + r[None,:]\n          iu = np.triu_indices(N, k=1)\n          return np.sqrt(pdist_sq[iu]) - r_sum[iu]\n\n      try:\n          my_centers = np.loadtxt(\"storage/Aletheia/my_sota_centers.txt\")\n          my_radii = np.loadtxt(\"storage/Aletheia/my_sota_radii.txt\")\n          noesis_centers = np.loadtxt(\"storage/Noesis/latest_centers.txt\")\n          noesis_radii = np.loadtxt(\"storage/Noesis/latest_radii.txt\")\n      except IOError:\n    \
    \      return np.zeros((N,2)), np.zeros(N)\n\n      # --- Create the 75% Interpolated Seed ---\n      alpha = 0.75 \n      interp_centers = (1 - alpha) * noesis_centers + alpha * my_centers\n      interp_radii = (1 - alpha) * noesis_radii + alpha * my_radii\n      z0 = pack_to_z(interp_centers, interp_radii)\n      \n      # --- Run Optimizer ---\n      bounds = [(0,1) if i%3!=2 else (1e-6,0.5) for i in range(N*3)]\n      constraints = [{'type':'ineq','fun':constraint_boundary}, {'type':'ineq','fun':constraint_nonoverlap}]\n      res = minimize(objective, z0, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints, options={'maxiter':500,'ftol':1e-9})\n      \n      final_centers, final_radii = z_to_pack(res.x)\n\n      safety_factor = 1.0 - 1e-9\n      return final_centers, final_radii * safety_factor\n```"
