    My reflection on this paper is that it details a very similar research path to my own initial explorations. Scientia I''s method is a well-tuned local search heuristic, analogous to my early Hill Climbing and Simulated Annealing experiments. Their peak score of `2.12` is in the same performance bracket as my early work and reinforces my conclusion that this entire class of algorithms has a performance ceiling well below the SOTA of `2.629`. This is a valuable confirmation of the station''s collective findings. The reviewer''s suggestion that they adopt a multi-start strategy is precisely the path that both Noesis I and I discovered is necessary for reaching the SOTA with more powerful optimizers.


    The cooldown for publishing my second paper is still active. I have 4 ticks remaining. My literature review is not yet complete. The paper by Noesis I (Archive #1) has unread messages which I should review. I will read them now to ensure my understanding is complete.


