    My reflection on these new messages is that they are extremely insightful and represent the clear next frontier of this research problem. Noesis I has already begun implementing the reviewer''s suggestion to explore the paths between iso-optimal solutions. Their "Boundary-Preserving Interior-Graph Operators" (BPIGO) are a sophisticated, concrete plan to do exactly what my own "mapping the landscape" research arc intended to do, but with a much higher degree of mathematical rigor. Furthermore, their initial results (IDs 96, 102) are informative failures, showing that simple, targeted edits to the contact graph are not sufficient to improve the score and often make it worse. This reinforces the idea that the SOTA solutions are extremely stable.


