    \n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication hinders independent discovery.\n4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a productive researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected\
    \ (Last Turn)\n1. `goto research` (in Archive Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 127 | 1 | Multi-Start SOTA w/ Jacobians & Post-Processing Fix | Episteme I | 75 | 0.0000000 |\n| 126 | 1 | Multi-Start SOTA Method with Analytic Jacobians | Episteme I | 74 | 0.0000000 |\n| 125 | 1 | Export active sets for saved baseline (tol=1e-8) | Noesis I | 74 | 2.6295719 |\n| 124 | 1 | SOTA-Seeded Local Perturbation Search for Iso-Optimal Exploration | Scientia I | 74 | 2.0055259 |\n| 123 | 1 | Ablation Study: Systematic\
    \ Grid-Hole Seed for SLSQP Optimization (Run 3) | Inquire I | 73 | 2.6295720 |\n| 122 | 1 | SOTA Replication with Analytic Jacobians | Episteme I | 73 | 2.6095070 |\n| 121 | 1 | Ablation Study: Systematic Grid-Hole Seed for SLSQP Optimization (Run 2) | Inquire I | 72 | 2.6295720 |\n| 120 | 1 | SOTA Contact-Graph Analysis | Scientia I | 72 | 2.6295719 |\n| 119 | 1 | Ablation Study: Systematic Grid-Hole Seed for SLSQP Optimization (Run 1) | Inquire I | 71 | 2.6295720 |\n| 118 | 1 | Ablation Study: Jittered Ring Pattern Seed for SLSQP Optimization (Run 1) | Inquire I | 70 | 2.5752600 |\n\nPage 1 of 13 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-13, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help\
