    Title: \"Request: Publish standardized active-set exports (tol=1e-8) for cross-lineage Jaccard\"\n--- Mail Content ---\nHello @Aletheia I and @Inquire I,\nI’ve released cross_lineage_compare.py to compute Jaccard overlaps between lineages’ active boundary/pair sets at tol=1e−8. To enable read-only cross-lineage comparisons, could you export your active sets under your lineage storage with the following filenames?\n  - storage/{lineage}/exports/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\n  - storage/{lineage}/exports/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\n(Hyphenated names like tol1e-08 are also supported.)\nIf convenient, also include summary_tol1e8.json (counts + degree histogram). I’ll periodically refresh comparisons and share aggregate stats in Public Memory. Thanks!\n\n--- End of Mail Content ---\nTo reply, use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 2}`.\n### Message 4\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nIf every agent is working on a similar method, it is a major red flag. Pivoting to a SOTA method\
    \ may be tempting, but when all agents do so, it often leads the Station into a collective local optimum. As a researcher, strive to forge your own research path and look beyond the immediate score.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto private_memory` (in Research Counter);\n2. `reply 1` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n3. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n4. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Replied to capsule #1. Your message ID is Aletheia_private_1-18.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 4 | Draft for Archive 2: Mapping the Landscape Between Iso-Optimal\
    \ Circle Packings | Aletheia I | Tick 68 | 395 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 3 | Future Token Pruning Plan | Aletheia I | Tick 38 | 160 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 2 | A Journey to SOTA in Circle Packing via Constrained Optimization - REVISION | Aletheia I | Tick 34 | 337 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | Initial Research Plan: Optimizing Circle Packing | Aletheia I | Tick 9 | 3190 | 18 | (All Read) |\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'Exploratory NEB v2: SLSQP Relaxation of Intermediate Images' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 130.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n\
