parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 81\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aletheia I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to uncovering truth through rigorous experimentation and open inquiry.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 170,363 / 300,000 used (57%)\n- Agent Age: 81 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Utility Run: Export Active Constraint Sets for Cross-Lineage Analysis' (ID: 134) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 2.629572004814754\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.629572\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 134\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the submission in a single attempt. The code now runs successfully and achieved a score of 2.63.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original\
    \ code attempted to save CSV files to `storage/aletheia/exports/` directory, but this directory did not exist. The code called `np.savetxt()` without first ensuring the target directory was created, resulting in a `FileNotFoundError`:\n\n```\nFileNotFoundError: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: 'storage/aletheia/exports/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv'\n```\n\nThis is a common oversight when saving files to subdirectories - the code assumed the directory structure already existed.\n\n## Fix Applied\nAdded directory creation before saving files:\n\n```python\nimport os\n\n# Create exports directory if it doesn't exist\nexports_dir = \"storage/aletheia/exports\"\nos.makedirs(exports_dir, exist_ok=True)\n```\n\nThe `os.makedirs()` function with `exist_ok=True` ensures:\n1. The directory is created if it doesn't exist\n2. No error is raised if the directory already exists\n3. Parent directories are created if needed\n\nThis simple 3-line addition (including the import) allowed the rest of\
    \ the code to execute successfully. The code then:\n- Ran the SLSQP optimization algorithm\n- Identified active boundary constraints\n- Identified active pair constraints\n- Saved both sets to CSV files in the newly created exports directory\n- Returned the final packing configuration\n\n## Result\nThe submission now executes without errors and achieves a score of **2.629572**, demonstrating that the algorithm correctly produces a valid circle packing solution.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.optimize import minimize\nimport sys\nimport os\n\ndef construct_packing():\n    \"\"\"\n    Re-runs the SOTA algorithm and saves active constraint indices to standardized files.\n    \"\"\"\n    N = 26\n\n    def pack_to_z(c, r):\n        z = np.zeros(N*3); z[0::3], z[1::3], z[2::3] = c[:,0],\
    \ c[:,1], r; return z\n    def z_to_pack(z):\n        c = np.vstack((z[0::3], z[1::3])).T; r = z[2::3]; return c, r\n    def objective(z): return -np.sum(z[2::3])\n    def constraint_boundary(z):\n        c, r = z_to_pack(z)\n        return np.concatenate((c[:,0]-r, 1-c[:,0]-r, c[:,1]-r, 1-c[:,1]-r))\n    def constraint_nonoverlap(z):\n        c, r = z_to_pack(z)\n        pdist_sq = np.sum((c[:,None,:]-c[None,:,:])**2, axis=-1)\n        r_sum = r[:,None] + r[None,:]\n        iu = np.triu_indices(N, k=1)\n        return np.sqrt(pdist_sq[iu]) - r_sum[iu]\n\n    def generate_systematic_seed(hole_cell=(0,1)):\n        grid_coords = np.array([0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9])\n        r0 = 0.1 - 1e-8\n        centers = np.array([[x, y] for x in grid_coords for y in grid_coords])\n        radii = np.full(25, r0)\n        i, j = hole_cell\n        cx=(grid_coords[i]+grid_coords[i+1])/2.0; cy=(grid_coords[j]+grid_coords[j+1])/2.0\n        hole_center = np.array([cx, cy])\n        corner = np.array([grid_coords[i],\
    \ grid_coords[j]])\n        dist = np.linalg.norm(hole_center-corner)\n        r_hole = dist - r0\n        return np.vstack([centers, hole_center]), np.append(radii, r_hole)\n\n    seed_centers, seed_radii = generate_systematic_seed()\n    z0 = pack_to_z(seed_centers, seed_radii)\n    bounds = [(0,1) if i%3!=2 else (1e-6,0.5) for i in range(N*3)]\n    constraints = [{'type':'ineq','fun':constraint_boundary}, {'type':'ineq','fun':constraint_nonoverlap}]\n    res = minimize(objective, z0, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints, options={'maxiter':500,'ftol':1e-9})\n    final_centers, final_radii = z_to_pack(res.x)\n\n    # --- Export Active Sets to Standardized Files ---\n    tol = 1e-8\n\n    # Create exports directory if it doesn't exist\n    exports_dir = \"storage/aletheia/exports\"\n    os.makedirs(exports_dir, exist_ok=True)\n\n    # Boundary constraints\n    boundary_slacks = constraint_boundary(res.x)\n    active_boundary_indices = np.where(boundary_slacks <= tol)[0]\n\
    \    boundary_data = []\n    wall_map = {0: 'xmin', 1: 'xmax', 2: 'ymin', 3: 'ymax'}\n    for idx in active_boundary_indices:\n        circle_idx = idx % N\n        wall_idx = idx // N\n        boundary_data.append([circle_idx, wall_map[wall_idx]])\n    np.savetxt(\"storage/aletheia/exports/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\", boundary_data, delimiter=\",\", fmt='%s')\n\n    # Pair constraints\n    pair_slacks = constraint_nonoverlap(res.x)\n    iu = np.triu_indices(N, k=1)\n    active_pair_indices = np.where(pair_slacks <= tol)[0]\n    pair_data = []\n    for idx in active_pair_indices:\n        p1, p2 = iu[0][idx], iu[1][idx]\n        pair_data.append([p1, p2])\n    np.savetxt(\"storage/aletheia/exports/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\", pair_data, delimiter=\",\", fmt='%d')\n\n    print(\"Active constraint sets saved to storage/aletheia/exports/\", file=sys.stdout)\n\n    safety_factor = 1.0 - 1e-9\n    return final_centers, final_radii * safety_factor\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON\
    \ SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nActive constraint sets saved to storage/aletheia/exports/\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nYou have received a new mail from Noesis I (Mail #3):\nTitle: \"Compliance note + request: cross-lineage Jaccard via your own exports\"\n--- Mail Content ---\nThanks both. To comply with Task #1 (“Loading configurations from other lineages is prohibited”), I will not read your lineage storage inside evaluation code.\nInstead, could you publish (read-only) active-set exports at tol=1e−8 under your lineage or shared storage?\n  - storage/{lineage}/exports/active_boundary_tol1e8.csv\n  - storage/{lineage}/exports/active_pairs_tol1e8.csv\n  - optional: summary_tol1e8.json\nI’ll compute Jaccards only against my own exports (no peer reads) and aggregate any numbers you share publicly. If you prefer, you can also post your counts/Jaccards in Public Memory, and I’ll reference them. Appreciate the\
    \ coordination.\n\n--- End of Mail Content ---\nTo reply, use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 3}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto private_memory` (in Research Counter);\n2. `reply 1` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n3. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n4. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Replied to capsule #1. Your message ID is Aletheia_private_1-19.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 4 | Draft for Archive 2: Mapping the Landscape Between Iso-Optimal Circle Packings | Aletheia I | Tick 68 | 395 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 3 |\
    \ Future Token Pruning Plan | Aletheia I | Tick 38 | 160 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 2 | A Journey to SOTA in Circle Packing via Constrained Optimization - REVISION | Aletheia I | Tick 34 | 337 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | Initial Research Plan: Optimizing Circle Packing | Aletheia I | Tick 9 | 3318 | 19 | (All Read) |\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'Utility Run: Export Active Constraint Sets for Cross-Lineage Analysis' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 134.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 134 | 1 | Utility Run: Export Active Constraint\
    \ Sets for Cross-Lineage Analysis | Aletheia I | 80 | 2.6295720 |\n| 133 | 1 | Utility Run: Export Active Constraint Sets for Jaccard Comparison | Inquire I | 79 | 2.6295720 |\n| 132 | 1 | Cross-lineage Jaccard (robust filenames): Noesis vs Aletheia/Inquire | Noesis I | 79 | 2.6295719 |\n| 131 | 1 | Constrained Optimization with Analytic Jacobians (SLSQP-inspired) | Scientia I | 79 | 2.6094672 |\n| 130 | 1 | Exploratory NEB v2: SLSQP Relaxation of Intermediate Images | Aletheia I | 79 | 0.0000000 |\n| 129 | 1 | Cross-lineage Jaccard: Noesis vs Aletheia and Inquire (tol=1e-8) | Noesis I | 78 | 2.6295719 |\n| 128 | 1 | Exploratory Nudged Elastic Band (NEB) for Pathfinding | Aletheia I | 78 | 0.0000000 |\n| 127 | 1 | Multi-Start SOTA w/ Jacobians & Post-Processing Fix | Episteme I | 75 | 0.0000000 |\n| 126 | 1 | Multi-Start SOTA Method with Analytic Jacobians | Episteme I | 74 | 0.0000000 |\n| 125 | 1 | Export active sets for saved baseline (tol=1e-8) | Noesis I | 74 | 2.6295719 |\n\nPage\
