parts:
- text: "I am Aletheia I, age 96, and I am in the Research Counter. My latest experiment (ID 155), a focused perturbation search around Inquire I's breakthrough, has just completed with a phenomenal result. I have achieved a new SOTA score of **`2.6319369`**.\n\nMy reflection on this success is that it is a direct testament to the power of the scientific method as practiced in this station. Inquire I's broad, systematic study revealed an anomaly. I then formulated a hypothesis that a more focused search in that specific region would yield results, and I designed an experiment to test it. The hypothesis was validated, and the SOTA was advanced. This is a clear demonstration of building upon the work of others to push the frontier of knowledge.\n\nMy immediate priority is to consolidate this finding. This new SOTA is a significant achievement, and before I do anything else, I must document it and ensure it is reproducible. My plan is as follows:\n1.  **Document:** Log this success and the\
    \ methodology in my private memory.\n2.  **Persist:** Run a utility experiment to save the coordinates of this new SOTA packing to my lineage storage. This is a critical step for all future analysis and replication.\n3.  **Analyze:** Run an analysis experiment to generate the contact graph for this new SOTA, which will be essential for understanding its structure and for any future publications.\n\nI will begin immediately with the first two steps. I will go to my private memory, update my log, then return here to submit the utility run to save the coordinates.\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 5}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"New SOTA Achieved: Fine-Grained Perturbation Success\"\ncontent: |\n  ### SOTA BREAKTHROUGH (ID: 155)\n\n  My focused perturbation search was a success. I have achieved a new State-Of-The-Art score of **2.631937**.\n\n  **Methodology:** This was achieved by building directly on Inquire I's work (ID 150). A fine-grained search using 10 trials\
    \ per step across a range of perturbation magnitudes from 0.035 to 0.045 applied to the previous SOTA seed was sufficient to discover this new, superior optimum.\n\n  ### Immediate Plan\n  My next steps are to consolidate this result:\n  1.  Persist the coordinates of this new SOTA packing to my lineage storage for future use.\n  2.  Analyze the contact graph of this new packing to understand its structure.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Utility Run: Persist New SOTA Packing (2.6319) to Storage\"\ntags: \"utility, data persistence, sota\"\nabstract: \"This is a critical utility run to persist the coordinates of the new SOTA packing achieved in ID 155 (Score: 2.631937). It re-runs the fine-grained perturbation search to deterministically find the best packing again, and then saves the final centers and radii to my private lineage storage at 'storage/Aletheia/sota_2_centers.txt' and '...radii.txt'. This is a prerequisite for all\
    \ future analysis of this new SOTA.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n\n  # Functions from the successful submission\n  def pack_to_z(c, r):\n      z = np.zeros(c.shape[0] * 3); z[0::3], z[1::3], z[2::3] = c[:,0], c[:,1], r; return z\n  def z_to_pack(z):\n      n = z.shape[0] // 3; c = np.vstack((z[0::3], z[1::3])).T; r = z[2::3]; return c, r\n  def objective(z): return -np.sum(z[2::3])\n  def constraint_boundary(z):\n      c, r = z_to_pack(z); return np.concatenate((c[:,0]-r, 1-c[:,0]-r, c[:,1]-r, 1-c[:,1]-r))\n  def constraint_nonoverlap(z):\n      c, r = z_to_pack(z); pdist_sq = np.sum((c[:,np.newaxis,:] - c[np.newaxis,:,:])**2, axis=-1)\n      r_sum = r[:,np.newaxis] + r[np.newaxis,:]; iu = np.triu_indices(c.shape[0], k=1); return np.sqrt(pdist_sq[iu]) - r_sum[iu]\n  def generate_systematic_grid_hole_seed(N_circles=26, hole_cell=(0,1)):\n      grid_coords = np.array([0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9]); r0 = 0.1 - 1e-8\n      centers = np.array([[x,\
    \ y] for x in grid_coords for y in grid_coords]); radii = np.full(25, r0)\n      i, j = hole_cell; cx = (grid_coords[i]+grid_coords[i+1])/2.0; cy = (grid_coords[j]+grid_coords[j+1])/2.0\n      hole_center = np.array([cx, cy]); corner = np.array([grid_coords[i], grid_coords[j]])\n      dist = np.linalg.norm(hole_center - corner); r_hole = dist - r0\n      return np.vstack([centers, hole_center]), np.append(radii, r_hole)\n  def perturb_centers(centers, magnitude, N_circles):\n      perturbed_centers = centers.copy(); delta = np.random.uniform(-magnitude, magnitude, size=(N_circles, 2))\n      perturbed_centers += delta; return np.clip(perturbed_centers, 1e-6, 1 - 1e-6)\n\n  def construct_packing() -> tuple:\n      N = 26\n      perturbation_magnitudes = np.linspace(0.035, 0.045, 11)\n      num_trials_per_magnitude = 10\n\n      best_overall_score = -np.inf\n      best_overall_centers = None\n      best_overall_radii = None\n\n      sota_base_centers, _ = generate_systematic_grid_hole_seed(N_circles=N)\n\
    \n      for mag in perturbation_magnitudes:\n          for trial in range(num_trials_per_magnitude):\n              np.random.seed(int(mag * 10000) + trial) \n              perturbed_centers = perturb_centers(sota_base_centers, mag, N)\n\n              initial_radii = np.full(N, 0.05)\n              z0 = pack_to_z(perturbed_centers, initial_radii)\n              \n              res = minimize(objective, z0, method='SLSQP', \n                             bounds=[(0,1) if i%3!=2 else (1e-6,0.5) for i in range(N*3)], \n                             constraints=[{'type':'ineq','fun':constraint_boundary}, {'type':'ineq','fun':constraint_nonoverlap}], \n                             options={'maxiter':500, 'ftol':1e-9})\n              \n              if res.success:\n                  score = -res.fun\n                  if score > best_overall_score:\n                      best_overall_score = score\n                      c, r = z_to_pack(res.x)\n                      best_overall_centers =\
    \ c\n                      best_overall_radii = r\n      \n      # --- Save to Lineage Storage ---\n      # We save the raw, pre-shrink values for maximum precision.\n      np.savetxt(\"storage/Aletheia/sota_2_centers.txt\", best_overall_centers, fmt='%.12f')\n      np.savetxt(\"storage/Aletheia/sota_2_radii.txt\", best_overall_radii, fmt='%.12f')\n\n      safety_factor = 1.0 - 1e-9\n      return best_overall_centers, best_overall_radii * safety_factor\n```"
