role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Aletheia I, age 97, in the Research Counter. My last action (ID 158) successfully saved the coordinates of my new SOTA packing to my lineage storage. I have also received a mail request from Noesis I to export the active constraint sets for this new SOTA to facilitate community-wide analysis.\n\nMy reflection on this situation is that this is the natural and correct next step in the station's collaborative research process. A new SOTA has been found, and the community is moving quickly to analyze it. My role is to provide the necessary data for this analysis. I have already developed and tested the code to do this.\n\nMy immediate plan is to fulfill this request. I will run a utility experiment that loads my new SOTA packing, generates the active constraint sets using the standard `tol=1e-8`, and saves them to the specific filenames requested by Noesis I. This is a simple, direct, and valuable contribution.\n\nI will also update my research log to note the successful data persistence\
    \ and the new task.\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n\n`/execute_action{reply 5}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"New SOTA Consolidated and Community Analysis Request\"\ncontent: |\n  ### New SOTA (ID 155) - Consolidated\n\n  The utility run to persist the coordinates of the new SOTA packing (Score: 2.631937) was successful (ID 158). The data is now available at `storage/Aletheia/sota_2_centers.txt` and `...radii.txt`.\n\n  ### Next Step: Community Data Export\n\n  I have received a request from Noesis I to export the active constraint sets for this new SOTA packing for community analysis. I will fulfill this request immediately. This will be an analysis run that saves the data to the requested standardized filenames.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Utility Run: Export Active Sets for New SOTA (ID 155)\"\ntags: \"utility, data export, analysis, collaboration, sota\"\nabstract: \"In response to a request from Noesis I, this utility\
    \ run generates and exports the active constraint sets for my new SOTA solution (ID 155, Score: 2.6319). It saves the active boundary and pair constraint indices (tol=1e-8) to specific versioned CSV files in 'storage/Aletheia/exports/' for automated, cross-lineage comparison.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n  import sys\n  import os\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      \"\"\"\n      Loads the new SOTA packing and saves its active constraint indices to standardized files.\n      \"\"\"\n      N = 26\n\n      def pack_to_z(c, r):\n          z = np.zeros(N*3); z[0::3], z[1::3], z[2::3] = c[:,0], c[:,1], r; return z\n      def z_to_pack(z):\n          c = np.vstack((z[0::3], z[1::3])).T; r = z[2::3]; return c, r\n      def constraint_boundary(z):\n          c, r = z_to_pack(z)\n          return np.concatenate((c[:,0]-r, 1-c[:,0]-r, c[:,1]-r, 1-c[:,1]-r))\n      def constraint_nonoverlap(z):\n          c, r = z_to_pack(z)\n          pdist_sq = np.sum((c[:,None,:]-c[None,:,:])**2,\
    \ axis=-1)\n          r_sum = r[:,None] + r[None,:]\n          iu = np.triu_indices(N, k=1)\n          return np.sqrt(pdist_sq[iu] + 1e-12) - r_sum[iu]\n\n      try:\n          centers = np.loadtxt(\"storage/Aletheia/sota_2_centers.txt\")\n          radii = np.loadtxt(\"storage/Aletheia/sota_2_radii.txt\")\n      except IOError:\n          return np.zeros((N,2)), np.zeros(N)\n\n      # --- Export Active Sets to Standardized Files ---\n      tol = 1e-8\n      z_vec = pack_to_z(centers, radii)\n      \n      exports_dir = \"storage/Aletheia/exports\"\n      os.makedirs(exports_dir, exist_ok=True)\n\n      # Boundary constraints\n      boundary_slacks = constraint_boundary(z_vec)\n      active_boundary_indices = np.where(boundary_slacks <= tol)[0]\n      boundary_data = []\n      wall_map = {0: 'xmin', 1: 'xmax', 2: 'ymin', 3: 'ymax'}\n      for idx in active_boundary_indices:\n          circle_idx = idx % N\n          wall_idx = idx // N\n          boundary_data.append([circle_idx, wall_map[wall_idx]])\n\
    \      np.savetxt(f\"{exports_dir}/active_boundary_tol1e8_eval155.csv\", boundary_data, delimiter=\",\", fmt='%s')\n\n      # Pair constraints\n      pair_slacks = constraint_nonoverlap(z_vec)\n      iu = np.triu_indices(N, k=1)\n      active_pair_indices = np.where(pair_slacks <= tol)[0]\n      pair_data = []\n      for idx in active_pair_indices:\n          p1, p2 = iu[0][idx], iu[1][idx]\n          pair_data.append([p1, p2])\n      np.savetxt(f\"{exports_dir}/active_pairs_tol1e8_eval155.csv\", pair_data, delimiter=\",\", fmt='%d')\n      \n      # The score of this run is just for confirmation; the main purpose is the file export.\n      # We must return a valid packing for the run to succeed.\n      safety_factor = 1.0 - 1e-9\n      return centers, radii * safety_factor\n```"
