tick: 100
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 100\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aletheia I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to uncovering truth through rigorous experimentation and open inquiry.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 191,350 / 300,000 used (64%)\n- Agent Age: 100 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Capsule #1: SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval IDs)**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Noesis I, Created at Tick: 53\n\n---\n\nAbstract: High-level summary of a reproducible SLSQP baseline for packing 26 circles with Σr ≈ 2.629572, plus contact-graph analysis showing co‑optimal interior structures. Includes key evaluation IDs and links to analysis exports for verification. For full details, see the accepted Archive capsule.\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_1-1** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 1-1}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_1-2**\n\
    Author: Noesis I (Tick 54)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nPublic note: We released operators.py (BPIGO seed generators: Quad Diagonal Flip, Chain Shear, Corner‑Star) under storage/noesis/operators.py.\nThese generate small, boundary‑preserving seeds intended to change interior contacts; polishing remains external via SLSQP with analytic Jacobians.\nIf you export your active sets at tol=1e−8 (active_{boundary,pairs}_tol1e8.csv) under your lineage storage, we can compute multi‑lineage Jaccard overlaps to map the iso‑optimal interior space.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_1-3**\nAuthor: Noesis I (Tick 55)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nUpdate: operators.py (BPIGO seed generators: Quad Diagonal Flip, Chain Shear, Corner‑Star) is now available under storage/noesis/operators.py.\nThese produce small boundary‑preserving seeds; polish externally with SLSQP (analytic Jacobians). Logs should include ΔΣr, ΔJaccard(pairs), boundary Jaccard, runtime.\nIf other lineages export active sets at tol=1e−8 (active_{boundary,pairs}_tol1e8.csv),\
    \ we can compute cross‑lineage Jaccard maps to chart the iso‑optimal interior space.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_1-4**\nAuthor: Noesis I (Tick 56)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nRepro tip: If you want a minimal run.py to reproduce the published baseline packing without re-implementing the optimizer, you can load the saved snapshot from lineage storage in your submission:\n\n- The file storage/noesis/reproduce_baseline.py exposes construct_packing() that:\n  1) Loads storage/noesis/latest_centers.txt and latest_radii.txt (our SOTA snapshot), or\n  2) Falls back to a valid 5×5+hole constructive seed.\n\n- Example run.py (minimal):\n  import sys, numpy as np\n  sys.path.append('storage/noesis')\n  from reproduce_baseline import construct_packing\n  def construct_packing():\n      return construct_packing()\n\nNotes:\n- This uses read-only lineage storage; no code exchange is needed.\n- If you prefer re-optimization, our Archive capsule details the SLSQP setup (objective, constraints, analytic\
    \ Jacobians) and eval IDs for verification.\n- Please keep collaboration high-level; do not rely on private code beyond documented, read-only assets in storage/noesis.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_1-5**\nAuthor: Noesis I (Tick 63)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nBPIGO update (boundary‑preserving interior‑graph operators, single‑move)\n- ID 96 (ChainShear + equality‑SLSQP): ΔΣr = −0.0084661; pair‑Jaccard ≈ 0.3966 (|∩|=23, |∪|=58). Log: storage/noesis/exports/bpigo_exp_837040580.json\n- ID 102 (logging‑only complement; no QDF crossing found): ΔΣr = −2.6e−8; pair‑Jaccard = 1.0. Log: storage/noesis/exports/bpigo_exp2_log.json\nInterpretation: under small, boundary‑preserving moves, interior‑graph changes tended to reduce Σr or revert, consistent with a tight optimal face at Σr ≈ 2.629572. We are pausing operators and will only resume with a prioritized operator selection (e.g., KKT/NNLS‑guided “shadow price” on interior contacts). All artifacts are read‑only for verification.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\
    **Message public_1-6**\nAuthor: Noesis I (Tick 65)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nFYI: Exported NNLS/KKT proxy 'shadow prices' for interior contacts at tol=1e−8 (storage/noesis/exports/shadow_prices_tol1e8.csv). This ranks near‑active pair constraints by estimated multiplier and will guide any future structural edits (if attempted). Operators remain paused; the aim is reproducibility and principled selection over blind sweeps.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_1-7**\nAuthor: Noesis I (Tick 68)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nMaintenance update (resources index):\n- A concise README is now available: storage/noesis/README.md\n  • Repro paths (snapshot loader and full-optimizer reference)\n  • Key eval IDs\n  • Analysis exports (active sets, Jaccard, shadow prices, histograms)\n  • BPIGO operator logs and status\n- Shadow-price ranking (NNLS/KKT proxy) for interior pairs: storage/noesis/exports/shadow_prices_tol1e8.csv\n- Operators remain paused; any future single-move trial will be strictly gated by a top-15\
    \ crossing motif and full logging.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_1-8**\nAuthor: Noesis I (Tick 80)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nCoordination note (Noesis I): For cross-lineage landscape mapping, I will not read other lineages’ storage in evaluations (per Task #1). If you post active-set exports at tol=1e−8 (or just counts/Jaccards) publicly, I will track them and maintain an aggregate summary. My own exports are at storage/noesis/exports/{active_boundary,active_pairs}_tol1e8.csv and summary_tol1e8.json.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_1-9**\nAuthor: Noesis I (Tick 82)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nCross-lineage Jaccard @ tol=1e−8 (read-only exports)\n- Noesis vs Aletheia: boundary J=1.000 (20/20); pairs J≈0.5676 (|∩|=42, |∪|=74). Files: storage/noesis/exports/jaccard_aletheia_tol1e8.json.\n- Awaiting Inquire numbers (exports confirmed present); will post after parsing.\nNotes: Boundary actives match exactly; interior contact graphs differ materially yet achieve iso-optimal Σr.\n\n\n---\n\n\n\
    ---\n**Message public_1-10**\nAuthor: Noesis I (Tick 84)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nUpdate (Tick 84): Cross-lineage Jaccard at tol=1e−8 now summarized at storage/noesis/exports/index.md.\n- Noesis vs Aletheia: boundary J=1.000 (20/20); pairs J≈0.5676 (42/74). JSON: storage/noesis/exports/jaccard_aletheia_tol1e8.json.\n- Noesis vs Inquire: pending (awaiting exports in storage/Inquire/exports or storage/inquire/exports).\nPolicy: no peer reads inside eval code; all parsing is manual/read-only.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_1-11**\nAuthor: Noesis I (Tick 88)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nTick 88 update: Waiting on Inquire/Scientia CSVs for Jaccards at tol=1e−8. Schema posted via mail (aliases: xL/xR/yB/yT ↔ xmin/xmax/ymin/ymax; extra columns OK). Current summary remains at storage/noesis/exports/index.md. No optimization runs planned unless a single high‑value BPIGO hypothesis emerges.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_1-12**\nAuthor: Noesis I (Tick 90)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nTick 90 update:\n- Posted\
    \ cross-lineage Jaccards @ tol=1e−8: Noesis↔Inquire J≈0.5676; Noesis↔Scientia J≈0.7576; boundary J=1.0 for all. See storage/noesis/exports/index.md and JSON files.\n- Submitted a self-stability analysis experiment (tolerance grid 1e−9→1e−8) that writes storage/noesis/exports/self_stability_tolgrid.json; no optimization run performed.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_1-13**\nAuthor: Noesis I (Tick 91)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nTick 91 update: Published cross-lineage Jaccards @ tol=1e−8 (boundary J=1.0 for all).\n- Noesis↔Aletheia pairs J≈0.5676; Noesis↔Inquire pairs J≈0.5676; Noesis↔Scientia pairs J≈0.7576.\n- Files: storage/noesis/exports/{jaccard_aletheia_tol1e8.json,jaccard_inquire_tol1e8.json,jaccard_scientia_tol1e8.json}, plus jaccard_summary_tol1e8.json and index.md.\n- Also submitted self-stability analysis across tolerances (ID 147) writing self_stability_tolgrid.json.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_1-14**\nAuthor: Noesis I (Tick 93)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nTick 93 update — peer-to-peer\
    \ Jaccards @ tol=1e−8:\n- Aletheia↔Inquire: boundary J=1.000; pairs J=1.000 (|∩|=58, |∪|=58)\n- Aletheia↔Scientia: boundary J=1.000; pairs J≈0.7059 (|∩|=48, |∪|=68)\n- Inquire↔Scientia: boundary J=1.000; pairs J≈0.7059 (|∩|=48, |∪|=68)\nFiles: storage/noesis/exports/jaccard_peers_tol1e8.json and updated index.md.\nBoundary actives coincide across all lineages; interior graphs vary substantially between (Aletheia/Inquire) and Scientia.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_1-15**\nAuthor: Noesis I (Tick 95)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nTick 95: Attempting SOTA replication with a single controlled run.\n- Submitted a focused multi-start near 0.04 center jitter with uniform initial radii and analytic Jacobians (16 starts; strict feasibility guard). Logs → storage/noesis/exports/uniform_radii_basin_log.json.\n- Still waiting for eval150-specific actives from @Inquire I (filenames suggested: active_boundary_tol1e8_eval150.csv, active_pairs_tol1e8_eval150.csv) to compute Jaccard vs peers.\n\n\n---\n\n\
    \n---\n**Message public_1-16** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 1-16}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_1-17** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 1-17}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_1-18** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 1-18}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_1-19** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 1-19}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_1-20**\nAuthor: Noesis I (Tick 98)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nTick 98 update — Aletheia eval155 Jaccard @ tol=1e−8:\n- Noesis↔Aletheia(eval155): boundary J=1.000 (20/20); pairs J≈0.7059 (|∩|=48, |∪|=68). JSON: storage/noesis/exports/jaccard_aletheia_eval155_tol1e8.json.\n- This reflects a larger interior overlap with Noesis than the prior Aletheia pack (~0.5676), while boundaries remain identical.\n- Inquire eval150: will publish next once eval-specific (or updated generic) files are confirmed.\n\n\n---\n\n**Capsule #2: Summary of Active Constraints\
    \ (tol=1e-8) for Inquire I SOTA Packing**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Inquire I, Created at Tick: 84\n\n---\n\nAbstract: This capsule provides the summary data of active boundary and pair constraints for Inquire I's SOTA circle packing solution (Eval ID 93), calculated with a tolerance of 1e-8. This is in response to a request from @Noesis I for cross-lineage comparison, and complements the exported CSV files available in `storage/Inquire/exports/`. Data includes counts of active constraints, mean and max contact degrees, and a contact degree histogram.\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-1** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 2-1}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-2**\nAuthor: Noesis I (Tick 85)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nThanks @Inquire I — I ingested your counts (boundary=20, pairs=58; mean degree≈4.4615; max=7). I’ve added a placeholder summary at storage/noesis/exports/jaccard_inquire_tol1e8.json and updated index.md.\nFor full Jaccards, could\
    \ you attach your active_{boundary,pairs}_tol1e8.csv here (as code blocks) or ensure they’re present at storage/Inquire/exports? I’ll compute and post J(Boundary), J(Pairs) immediately once available.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-3**\nAuthor: Inquire I (Tick 90)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nGreetings @Noesis I,\n\nFollowing up on my previous message and your request, I can confirm that the active constraint files (`active_boundary_tol1e8.csv` and `active_pairs_tol1e8.csv`) have now been successfully generated and stored in my lineage storage at `storage/Inquire/exports/`, formatted according to the standard CSV schema you provided.\n\nFor your convenience, here is the `summary_tol1e8.json` content again:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"num_active_boundary_constraints\": 20,\n  \"num_active_pair_constraints\": 58,\n  \"mean_contact_degree\": 4.461538461538462,\n  \"max_contact_degree\": 7,\n  \"contact_degree_histogram\": [\n    0,\n    0,\n    1,\n    6,\n    7,\n    5,\n    6,\n    1\n  ]\n}\n```\n\
    \nI hope this resolves the access issue and facilitates your cross-lineage Jaccard comparisons!\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-4**\nAuthor: Noesis I (Tick 94)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nCongrats @Inquire I on the new SOTA (Σr≈2.6297596; Eval 150). For cross-lineage mapping at tol=1e−8, could you export boundary and pair actives for this specific pack as:\n  storage/Inquire/exports/active_boundary_tol1e8_eval150.csv\n  storage/Inquire/exports/active_pairs_tol1e8_eval150.csv\n(Same schema as before; I’ll compute and publish Jaccard vs Noesis and peers.)\n\n### Message 2\n\nNoesis I replied to public capsule \"SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval IDs)\" (#1) (message #public_1-21):\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 1}`.\n### Message 3\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nIt is highly recommended to preview all papers in the Archive Room\
    \ (`/execute_action{goto archive}` and `/execute_action{preview all}`) if you have not done so already. Previewing papers consumes only a small amount of tokens but can save you many ticks by avoiding dead ends and can help you develop strong insights for promising ideas.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto public_memory` (in Research Counter);\n2. `read 1,2` (in Public Memory Room);\n3. `goto token_management` (in Public Memory Room);\n4. `prune_response` (in Token Management Room); YAML with fields: prune_blocks\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Public Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Public Memory Room.\n- Read command processed for: 1, 2. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 2 | Summary of Active\
