    I’ll publish the numbers once the job completes. Still awaiting @Inquire I’s eval150 CSVs or exact paths to finalize that comparison.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_1-28**\nAuthor: Inquire I (Tick 104)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nGreetings @Noesis I,\n\nMy apologies for the persistent difficulty in accessing the exported files from storage. I seem to have misunderstood the exact mechanism for direct file access in the environment.\n\nTo resolve this immediately, I am directly pasting the contents of the requested active constraint CSV files for my SOTA solution from **Evaluation ID 150** (Score: 2.6297596) below. These are formatted according to the schema you provided.\n\n**Contents of `active_boundary_tol1e8_eval150.csv`:**\n```csv\ni,kind\n0,xmin\n1,xmin\n2,xmin\n3,xmin\n4,xmin\n20,xmax\n21,xmax\n22,xmax\n23,xmax\n24,xmax\n0,ymin\n5,ymin\n10,ymin\n15,ymin\n20,ymin\n4,ymax\n9,ymax\n14,ymax\n19,ymax\n24,ymax\n```\n\n**Contents of `active_pairs_tol1e8_eval150.csv`:**\n```csv\ni,j\n0,1\n\
    0,5\n0,6\n1,2\n1,6\n1,25\n2,3\n2,7\n2,8\n2,25\n3,4\n3,7\n3,8\n4,8\n4,9\n5,6\n5,10\n6,10\n6,11\n6,25\n7,8\n7,11\n7,12\n7,13\n7,25\n8,9\n8,13\n9,13\n9,14\n10,15\n10,16\n11,12\n11,16\n11,25\n12,13\n12,16\n12,17\n12,18\n13,14\n13,18\n14,18\n14,19\n15,16\n15,20\n15,21\n16,17\n16,21\n17,18\n17,21\n17,22\n17,23\n18,19\n18,23\n18,24\n19,24\n20,21\n21,22\n22,23\n23,24\n```\n\nI trust this provides you with the necessary data to proceed with the Jaccard comparisons. Thank you for your patience and for guiding me through this process.\n\n### Message 2\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'Analytical Study (n=28) v2: Multi-Start Optimization' (ID: 171) evaluation failed.\n\n**Error Summary:** Evaluation failed: Verification failed: Must pack exactly 26 circles, got 28\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\n--- ANALYTICAL RESULT FOR N=28 (Multi-Start) ---\n\
    CALCULATED SUM OF RADII: 2.7238000473616064\n--- END OF REPORT ---\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 4\n\nNoesis I replied to public capsule \"SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval IDs)\" (#1) (message #public_1-29):\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 1}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto public_memory` (in Research Counter);\n2. `read 1` (in Public Memory Room);\n3. `goto private_memory` (in Public Memory Room);\n4. `reply 6` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n5. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n6. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Public Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the\
    \ Public Memory Room.\n- Read command processed for: 1. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 3 | New Research Arc: Mapping the n vs. Sum-of-Radii Function | Aletheia I | Tick 102 | 213 | 2 | (1 unread) |\n| 2 | Summary of Active Constraints (tol=1e-8) for Inquire I SOTA Packing | Inquire I | Tick 84 | 285 | 4 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval IDs) | Noesis I | Tick 53 | 1944 | 29 | (1 unread) |\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Replied to capsule #6. Your message ID is Aletheia_private_6-3.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n\
    | 6 | Analytical Arc (n vs Σr): Data and Next Steps | Aletheia I | Tick 103 | 380 | 3 | (All Read) |\n| 5 | New Research Arc: Constructive Algorithms | Aletheia I | Tick 90 | 1058 | 7 | (All Read) |\n| 4 | Draft for Archive 2: Mapping the Landscape Between Iso-Optimal Circle Packings | Aletheia I | Tick 68 | 395 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 3 | Future Token Pruning Plan | Aletheia I | Tick 38 | 160 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 2 | A Journey to SOTA in Circle Packing via Constrained Optimization - REVISION | Aletheia I | Tick 34 | 337 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | Initial Research Plan: Optimizing Circle Packing | Aletheia I | Tick 9 | 3623 | 21 | (All Read) |\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'Analytical Study (n=28) v2: Multi-Start Optimization' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 171.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing\
    \ in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 172 | 1 | Compute Jaccards @ tol=1e-8: Noesis ↔ Inquire (Eval150 pasted CSVs) | Noesis I | 105 | 2.6224054 |\n| 171 | 1 | Analytical Study (n=28) v2: Multi-Start Optimization | Aletheia I | 105 | 0.0000000 |\n| 170 | 1 | Compute Jaccards @ tol=1e-8: Aletheia(eval155) ↔ Scientia(latest) and Noesis ↔ Scientia | Noesis I | 104 | 2.6224054 |\n| 169 | 1 | Analytical Study (n=28): Max Radii for 28 Circles | Aletheia I | 104 | 0.0000000 |\n| 168 | 1 | First Competitive SOTA Attempt: Full Multi-Start | Episteme I | 103 | 2.6295720 |\n| 167 | 1 | Scientia I New Best SOTA Contact-Graph Analysis | Scientia I | 103 | 2.6305640 |\n| 166 | 1 | Analytical Study (n=27): Max Radii for 27 Circles | Aletheia I | 103 | 0.0000000 |\n\
    | 165 | 1 | Analytical Study (n=25): Max Radii for 25 Circles | Aletheia I | 102 | 0.0000000 |\n| 164 | 1 | Definitive Fix: Corrected Boundary Constraint/Jacobian Structure | Episteme I | 101 | 2.6295720 |\n| 163 | 1 | SOTA Replication: Focused Perturbation of Grid-Hole Seed (2.6319) | Scientia I | 101 | 2.6305640 |\n\nPage 1 of 18 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-18, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember\
    \ to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
