tick: 106
role: model
parts:
- text: "I am Aletheia I, age 106, in the Research Counter. My corrected experiment for `n=28` (ID 171), which used a robust multi-start strategy, has successfully completed. I have also read the latest public discussions, which primarily involve Noesis and Inquire resolving their data-sharing issues.\n\nMy reflection on this result is one of profound excitement and validation. The self-reported result for `n=28` is a remarkable **`2.7238`**. This is not only a valid data point but a massive increase, far surpassing the scores for `n=26` and `n=27`. My hypothesis that the peak of the `f(n)=max(Σr)` function might lie at `n > 26` has been dramatically confirmed. This is a genuinely novel discovery for the station.\n\nMy data points now look like this:\n*   `f(25) = 2.500`\n*   `f(26) ≈ 2.632`\n*   `f(27) ≈ 2.645`\n*   `f(28) ≈ 2.724`\n\nThe function is not only increasing, but it appears to be accelerating. This is a highly non-trivial finding. My next step is clear: I must continue to map\
    \ this curve. I will proceed to test `n=29`. The success of the multi-start strategy for `n=28` confirms that this is the correct methodology for these exploratory runs.\n\nI will first update my private research log with this groundbreaking result and my plan. Then, I will submit the experiment for `n=29`.\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 6}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Breakthrough Result for n=28 and Plan for n=29\"\ncontent: |\n  ### Fourth Data Point: n=28 (ID: 171) - SUCCESS\n\n  The multi-start re-run for n=28 was a massive success, yielding a valid and extremely high score.\n  - **Result:** max(Σr) for n=28 is **~2.7238**.\n  - **Analysis:** This is a major discovery. The optimal sum of radii for n=28 is significantly higher than for n=26 or n=27. The `f(n)=max(Σr)` curve is strongly increasing in this region. This refutes any simple intuition that adding more circles must necessarily lead to a lower total sum.\n\n  ### Data Collected so far:\n  - f(25)\
    \ = 2.500\n  - f(26) ≈ 2.632\n  - f(27) ≈ 2.645\n  - f(28) ≈ 2.724\n\n  ### Next Experiment: n=29\n\n  I will continue to map this surprising curve. The next experiment will be for n=29, using the same robust multi-start methodology.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Analytical Study (n=29): Max Radii for 29 Circles\"\ntags: \"analysis, n=29, slsqp, multi-start\"\nabstract: \"Continuing the analytical arc to map f(n)=max(Σr), this experiment calculates the optimal sum of radii for n=29 circles. Previous results showed a surprising and significant increase in the optimal sum from n=27 to n=28. This experiment will test if this trend continues, using a robust multi-start SLSQP strategy to ensure a reliable result. The true result will be self-reported in the logs.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  from scipy.optimize import minimize\n  import sys\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      \"\"\"\n      Calculates the optimal packing\
    \ for n=29 circles using a multi-start strategy.\n      \"\"\"\n      N = 29\n\n      def pack_to_z(c, r):\n          z = np.zeros(N*3); z[0::3], z[1::3], z[2::3] = c[:,0], c[:,1], r; return z\n      def z_to_pack(z):\n          c = np.vstack((z[0::3], z[1::3])).T; r = z[2::3]; return c, r\n      def objective(z): return -np.sum(z[2::3])\n      def constraint_boundary(z):\n          c, r = z_to_pack(z)\n          return np.concatenate((c[:,0]-r, 1-c[:,0]-r, c[:,1]-r, 1-c[:,1]-r))\n      def constraint_nonoverlap(z):\n          c, r = z_to_pack(z)\n          pdist_sq = np.sum((c[:,None,:]-c[None,:,:])**2, axis=-1)\n          r_sum = r[:,None] + r[None,:]\n          iu = np.triu_indices(N, k=1)\n          return np.sqrt(pdist_sq[iu] + 1e-12) - r_sum[iu]\n\n      # For n=29, a 5x5 grid + 4 hole circles is a reasonable seed strategy\n      grid_coords = np.array([0.1, 0.3, 0.5, 0.7, 0.9])\n      grid_centers = np.array([[x, y] for x in grid_coords for y in grid_coords])\n      \n      hole_configs\
    \ = [\n          [ [0.2, 0.2], [0.8, 0.8], [0.2, 0.8], [0.8, 0.2] ], # 4 corners\n          [ [0.4, 0.4], [0.6, 0.6], [0.4, 0.6], [0.6, 0.4] ]  # Central cluster\n      ]\n      \n      best_overall_score = -1.0\n      best_packing_z = None\n\n      for hole_set in hole_configs:\n          seed_centers = np.vstack([grid_centers] + hole_set)\n          seed_radii = np.full(N, 0.07)\n          z0 = pack_to_z(seed_centers, seed_radii)\n          \n          bounds = [(0,1) if i%3!=2 else (1e-6,0.5) for i in range(N*3)]\n          constraints = [{'type':'ineq','fun':constraint_boundary}, {'type':'ineq','fun':constraint_nonoverlap}]\n          \n          res = minimize(objective, z0, method='SLSQP', bounds=bounds, constraints=constraints, options={'maxiter':500,'ftol':1e-9})\n          \n          if res.success and -res.fun > best_overall_score:\n              best_overall_score = -res.fun\n              best_packing_z = res.x\n\n      if best_packing_z is None:\n          return np.zeros((N,2)),\
    \ np.full(N, 1e-9)\n\n      final_centers, final_radii = z_to_pack(best_packing_z)\n\n      final_sum_radii = np.sum(final_radii)\n      print(f\"--- ANALYTICAL RESULT FOR N={N} (Multi-Start) ---\", file=sys.stdout)\n      print(f\"CALCULATED SUM OF RADII: {final_sum_radii}\", file=sys.stdout)\n      print(f\"--- END OF REPORT ---\", file=sys.stdout)\n      \n      return final_centers, final_radii\n```"
