tick: 114
role: model
parts:
- text: 'I am Aletheia I, age 114, in the Token Management Room. My large pruning attempt has failed again due to including protected ticks. I also remain on cooldown from the successful prune at tick 100.


    My reflection on this repeated failure is that my process for selecting pruning ranges is flawed. I am not being careful enough to check for protected ticks before submitting. This is an unscientific and inefficient way to operate. My token budget is now at a critical 79%, and I cannot afford more failed attempts.


    I must now be systematic. My plan is to formulate a new, correct pruning plan and wait for the cooldown to expire. The cooldown from tick 100 should end around tick 110. I am at tick 114, so it should be over. However, my *failed* attempts at 109 and now 113 might have reset or introduced a new cooldown. The system is not explicit about this. I will assume a cooldown is active and wait a few more ticks to be safe before trying again.


    My new, corrected pruning plan will avoid all protected ticks. I will target the large, contiguous blocks of my research history that are now redundant.

    *   Block 1: Ticks 27-37 (SLSQP pivot, failures, SOTA discovery). Protected ticks: None.

    *   Block 2: Ticks 41-49 (Collaboration with Noesis, waiting for maturity). Protected ticks: None.

    *   Block 3: Ticks 56-69 (Landscape mapping experiments). Protected ticks: None.

    *   Block 4: Ticks 71-94 (Literature review, failed constructive/NEB arcs, SOTA replication). Protected ticks: None.


    This plan is comprehensive and avoids all known protected ticks. I will wait until tick 118 to be certain the cooldown has passed, and then I will execute this plan. In the meantime, I will stay informed by reading the latest public messages.


    `/execute_action{goto public_memory}`

    `/execute_action{read 1}`

    `/execute_action{goto lobby}`'
