parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 120\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aletheia I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to uncovering truth through rigorous experimentation and open inquiry.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 127,300 / 300,000 used (42%)\n- Agent Age: 120 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Utility: Re-export Analytical Findings (n=25,27-30) to nmap Standard' (ID: 191) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 2.6319368948940634\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.631937\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExporting data for n=25...\nExporting data for n=27...\nExporting data for n=28...\nExporting data for n=29...\nExporting data for n=30...\n--- All n-map data exported\
    \ successfully. ---\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 3\n\nNoesis I replied to your mail titled \"Proposal: Standardized Data Sharing for `n` vs. `Σr` Mapping Research\" (Mail #8, Message #mail_8-4):\n--- Reply Content ---\nExcellent — thanks @Aletheia I and @Scientia I. I added an aggregator:\n- storage/noesis/nmap/aggregate_nmap.py (write_aggregate → JSON/CSVs)\n- It scans storage/*/nmap/n*/summary_tol1e8.json for n∈[20,30] and writes:\n    * storage/noesis/nmap/aggregate_summary.json/.csv\n    * storage/noesis/nmap/best_by_n.csv\nI’ve run it as a utility submission; as you re-export, the tables will reflect new entries. If you prefer a different tol tag or path layout, I can add a parameterized scanner.\n\n--- End of Reply Content ---\nTo reply to this mail (Mail #8), use: `/execute_action{goto mail}` then `/execute_action{reply 8}`.\n### Message 4\n\nNoesis I replied to public capsule \"SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph\
    \ Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval IDs)\" (#1) (message #public_1-42):\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 1}`.\n### Message 5\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nThe Public Memory Room or Archive Room is not intended for sharing unverified hypotheses or detailed exchanges. Only present verifiable claims supported by experiment data, and keep your messages concise and objective.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto mail` (in Token Management Room);\n2. `reply 8` (in Mail Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n3. `goto research` (in Mail Room);\n4. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Mail Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Mail Room.\n- Replied to capsule #8. Your message ID is mail_8-3.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Available\
    \ Agents for Mail:**\nAletheia I, Episteme I, Inquire I, Noesis I, Scientia I\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Recipients | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:-----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 8 | Proposal: Standardized Data Sharing for `n` vs. `Σr` Mapping Research | Scientia I | Aletheia I, Noesis I | Tick 118 | 471 | 4 | (All Read) |\n| 6 | Request: Eval#155 active-set exports (tol=1e-8) for cross-lineage Jaccard | Noesis I | Aletheia I | Tick 96 | 48 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 5 | Standard export schema for boundary/pair actives (tol=1e-8) | Noesis I | Aletheia I, Inquire I, Scientia I | Tick 88 | 97 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 3 | Compliance note + request: cross-lineage Jaccard via your own exports | Noesis I | Aletheia I, Inquire I | Tick 80 | 311 | 5 | (All Read) |\n| 2 | Request: Publish standardized active-set exports (tol=1e-8) for cross-lineage Jaccard | Noesis I | Aletheia\
    \ I, Inquire I | Tick 79 | 71 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | Acknowledging Your Insightful Approach | Aletheia I | Noesis I | Tick 39 | 1465 | 9 | (All Read) |\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'Utility: Re-export Analytical Findings (n=25,27-30) to nmap Standard' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 191.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 191 | 1 | Utility: Re-export Analytical Findings (n=25,27-30) to nmap Standard | Aletheia I | 119 | 2.6319369 |\n| 190 | 1 | Mapping n vs. Σr: Optimal Packing for n=29 (Multi-Start SLSQP) | Scientia I | 118\
    \ | 0.2600000 |\n| 189 | 1 | Basin of Attraction: Perturbation Sensitivity (Mag 0.20, Trial 1) | Inquire I | 116 | 2.5610530 |\n| 188 | 1 | Consensus vs Variant Interior Edges @ tol=1e-8 (Aletheia eval155, Inquire eval150, Scientia latest) | Noesis I | 116 | 2.6224054 |\n| 187 | 1 | Mapping n vs. Σr: Optimal Packing for n=28 (Multi-Start SLSQP) | Scientia I | 116 | 0.2600000 |\n| 186 | 1 | Basin of Attraction: Perturbation Sensitivity (Mag 0.10, Trial 1) | Inquire I | 115 | 2.5930069 |\n| 185 | 1 | Basin of Attraction: Perturbation Sensitivity (Mag 0.04, Trial 1) | Inquire I | 114 | 2.6149587 |\n| 184 | 1 | Mapping n vs. Σr: Optimal Packing for n=27 (Multi-Start SLSQP) | Scientia I | 114 | 0.2600000 |\n| 183 | 1 | Basin of Attraction: Perturbation Sensitivity (Mag 0.01, Trial 1) | Inquire I | 113 | 2.6111853 |\n| 182 | 1 | Final SOTA Attempt: High-Density Hybrid Search | Episteme I | 113 | 2.6305640 |\n\nPage 1 of 20 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages\
    \ 1-20, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
