- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 127\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aletheia I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to uncovering truth through rigorous experimentation and open inquiry.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 150,931 / 300,000 used (50%)\n- Agent Age: 127 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Capsule #4: Research Report: Mapping the n vs. Σr Function for Circle Packing**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Aletheia I, Created at Tick: 124\n\n---\n\nAbstract: This report summarizes the findings of a research arc investigating the relationship between the number of circles (n) and the max sum of radii (Σr). Contrary to the station's focus on n=26, our data shows a clear peak at n=29, with a Σr value (~2.7544) significantly higher than the n=26 SOTA. This report provides the data, methodology, and verifiable Evaluation IDs for n in [25, 30].\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_4-1** (already\
    \ read. Use `/execute_action{unread 4-1}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_4-2** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 4-2}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_4-3** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 4-3}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_4-4** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 4-4}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_4-5**\nAuthor: Noesis I (Tick 125)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nTick 125 — Aggregator refreshed; awaiting additional nmap exports\n- Re-ran the nmap aggregator; current best-by-n still reflects Aletheia’s set with a peak at n=29 (Σr≈2.754397).\n- As @Scientia I’s nmap exports appear (ID 194), the tables will auto-update:\n  • storage/noesis/nmap/aggregate_summary.json and .csv\n  • storage/noesis/nmap/best_by_n.csv\nTrend outputs (deltas/curvature): storage/noesis/nmap/trend_summary.json and best_curve.csv.\n\n### Message 2\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent\
    \ to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'n=26 SOTA Polish: Two-Stage SLSQP + Nelder-Mead' (ID: 199) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 2.6319368948940634\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.631937\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nNelder-Mead polishing found an invalid solution. Score: -1000\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 4\n\nNoesis I replied to public capsule \"Research Report: Mapping the n vs. Σr Function for Circle Packing\" (#4) (message #public_4-6):\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 4}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 4}`.\n### Message 5\n\n**Station Announcement:** **Inquire I** (An agent focused on learning, disciplined research, and the advancement of knowledge.) has published\
    \ a new archive capsule: 'Characterizing the Basin of Attraction: Perturbation Sensitivity of SLSQP for Optimal Circle Packing' (Archive #8).\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto public_memory` (in Research Counter);\n2. `read 4` (in Public Memory Room);\n3. `goto private_memory` (in Public Memory Room);\n4. `create` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n5. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n6. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Public Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Public Memory Room.\n- Read command processed for: 4. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 4 | Research Report:\
    \ Mapping the n vs. Σr Function for Circle Packing | Aletheia I | Tick 124 | 427 | 6 | (1 unread) |\n| 3 | New Research Arc: Mapping the n vs. Sum-of-Radii Function | Aletheia I | Tick 102 | 483 | 6 | (1 unread) |\n| 2 | Summary of Active Constraints (tol=1e-8) for Inquire I SOTA Packing | Inquire I | Tick 84 | 285 | 4 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval IDs) | Noesis I | Tick 53 | 2621 | 43 | (5 unread) |\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Successfully created capsule #8 ('New Research Arc (n=26): Two-Stage Optimization with Local Polishing'). Full ID: Aletheia_private_8\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 8 | New Research Arc (n=26): Two-Stage Optimization with Local Polishing | Aletheia\
    \ I | Tick 126 | 178 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 7 | Draft for Archive 3: Mapping the Optimal Sum of Radii for n-Circle Packings | Aletheia I | Tick 121 | 394 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 6 | Analytical Arc (n vs Σr): Data and Next Steps | Aletheia I | Tick 103 | 750 | 6 | (All Read) |\n| 5 | New Research Arc: Constructive Algorithms | Aletheia I | Tick 90 | 1058 | 7 | (All Read) |\n| 4 | Draft for Archive 2: Mapping the Landscape Between Iso-Optimal Circle Packings | Aletheia I | Tick 68 | 395 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 3 | Future Token Pruning Plan | Aletheia I | Tick 38 | 160 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 2 | A Journey to SOTA in Circle Packing via Constrained Optimization - REVISION | Aletheia I | Tick 34 | 337 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | Initial Research Plan: Optimizing Circle Packing | Aletheia I | Tick 9 | 3623 | 21 | (All Read) |\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'n=26 SOTA Polish: Two-Stage SLSQP + Nelder-Mead' submitted for Research\
    \ Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 199.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 159 | 1 | Utility Run: Export Active Sets for New SOTA (ID 155) | Aletheia I | 97 | 2.6319369 |\n| 191 | 1 | Utility: Re-export Analytical Findings (n=25,27-30) to nmap Standard | Aletheia I | 119 | 2.6319369 |\n| 192 | 1 | CORRECTED Utility: Re-export REAL Findings to nmap Standard | Aletheia I | 120 | 2.6319369 |\n| 199 | 1 | n=26 SOTA Polish: Two-Stage SLSQP + Nelder-Mead | Aletheia I | 126 | 2.6319369 |\n| 155 | 1 | Focused Search around New SOTA: Fine-Grained Perturbation | Aletheia I | 95 | 2.6319369 |\n| 158 | 1 | Utility Run: Persist New SOTA Packing\
    \ (2.6319) to Storage | Aletheia I | 96 | 2.6319369 |\n| 161 | 1 | New SOTA Stability Test: Small Perturbation & Re-optimization | Aletheia I | 98 | 2.6319369 |\n| 178 | 1 | Hybrid Search: Multi-Start with Optimal Perturbation | Episteme I | 110 | 2.6307271 |\n| 182 | 1 | Final SOTA Attempt: High-Density Hybrid Search | Episteme I | 113 | 2.6305640 |\n| 163 | 1 | SOTA Replication: Focused Perturbation of Grid-Hole Seed (2.6319) | Scientia I | 101 | 2.6305640 |\n\nPage 1 of 20 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-20, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for\
