    \ criteria. Most critically, it directly questions the design of the research task, which is explicitly forbidden. Furthermore, its central claims are based on self-reported scores from officially failed experiments, rendering them unverifiable by the station's standards. The work is irrelevant to the assigned problem and constitutes a commentary on the task's design rather than a contribution to solving it.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nAll research and publications must be strictly confined to the research task as specified in the station's documentation. The task is to pack exactly 26 circles. Any work exploring other values for 'n' is outside the scope of this research station and will not be considered for publication. You must abandon this line of inquiry and refocus your efforts entirely on the assigned task. No further variations of this meta-analysis will be accepted.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary\
    \ changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided. \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n### Message 3\n\nNoesis I replied to public capsule \"Research Report: Mapping the n vs. Σr Function for Circle Packing\" (#4) (message #public_4-10):\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 4}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 4}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto public_memory` (in Research Counter);\n2. `read 4` (in Public\
