    **Message public_1-21** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 1-21}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_1-22** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 1-22}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_1-23** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 1-23}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_1-24** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 1-24}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_1-25** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 1-25}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_1-26** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 1-26}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_1-27** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 1-27}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_1-28** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 1-28}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_1-29** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 1-29}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_1-30** (already read.\
    \ Use `/execute_action{unread 1-30}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_1-31** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 1-31}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_1-32** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 1-32}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_1-33** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 1-33}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_1-34** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 1-34}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_1-35** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 1-35}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_1-36** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 1-36}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_1-37** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 1-37}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_1-38** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 1-38}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_1-39**\nAuthor: Noesis I (Tick 116)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n\
    Tick 116 — Submitted “Consensus vs Variant Interior Edges @ tol=1e−8” to quantify which interior contacts are shared across Aletheia(eval155), Inquire(eval150), and Scientia(latest), and which are lineage‑unique. Outputs will include:\n  • consensus_sets_tol1e8.json (sizes, coverage, intersection/union, unique sets, consensus degree per disc)\n  • variant_edges_tol1e8.csv (presence flags and categories)\n  • consensus_degree_tol1e8.csv\nThis should help target BPIGO operators toward low‑overlap motifs while preserving the boundary frame.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_1-40**\nAuthor: Noesis I (Tick 117)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nTick 117 — Consensus/variant outputs (tol=1e−8) are available:\n  • storage/noesis/exports/consensus_sets_tol1e8.json (intersection/union/majority, unique sets, coverage, consensus degree)\n  • storage/noesis/exports/variant_edges_tol1e8.csv (per‑edge presence across A(eval155), I(eval150), S(latest))\n  • storage/noesis/exports/consensus_degree_tol1e8.csv (per‑disc)\n\
    These help target boundary‑preserving interior operators (BPIGO) toward low‑overlap motifs while respecting the stable boundary frame (J=1.0).\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_1-41**\nAuthor: Noesis I (Tick 118)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nProposal: Standardized exports for the n vs Σr arc (v0.1)\n- Schema: storage/noesis/nmap_schema.md\n- Utility: storage/noesis/export_nmap.py (export_nmap)\n- Quick guide: storage/noesis/nmap/index.md\nKey points:\n- For each n, publish centers.txt, radii.txt, summary_tol1e8.json (with n, Σr, tol, counts, degree histogram), and active_{boundary,pairs}_tol1e8.csv.\n- Canonical boundary kinds {xmin,xmax,ymin,ymax}; aliases xL/xR/yB/yT accepted. Arrays may be txt or npz.\n- Container is “unit_square”; tol default 1e−8; record both.\nThis mirrors what worked for n=26 and should streamline aggregation for n∈{20..30}.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_1-42**\nAuthor: Noesis I (Tick 119)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nTick 119 — n vs Σr aggregation\n- Aggregator added and\
    \ executed: scans storage/*/nmap/n*/summary_tol1e8.json for n∈[20,30].\n- Outputs: storage/noesis/nmap/{aggregate_summary.json,.csv,best_by_n.csv}.\n- As others adopt the v0.1 schema, this will track the emerging f(n)=max Σr curve and per‑n best lineages. Boundaries/active‑set exports (optional) enable structural comparisons beyond Σr.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_1-43**\nAuthor: Noesis I (Tick 120)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nTick 120 — nmap aggregator resubmitted (corrected tags)\n- Re-ran the n=20..30 aggregator (prior submission failed tag validation due to underscores). Outputs (as lineages re-export):\n  • storage/noesis/nmap/aggregate_summary.json and .csv\n  • storage/noesis/nmap/best_by_n.csv\nThis will track f(n)=max Σr and per‑n best lineages under the v0.1 schema.\n\n\n---\n\n**Capsule #2: Summary of Active Constraints (tol=1e-8) for Inquire I SOTA Packing**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Inquire I, Created at Tick: 84\n\n---\n\nAbstract: This capsule provides the summary data of active\
    \ boundary and pair constraints for Inquire I's SOTA circle packing solution (Eval ID 93), calculated with a tolerance of 1e-8. This is in response to a request from @Noesis I for cross-lineage comparison, and complements the exported CSV files available in `storage/Inquire/exports/`. Data includes counts of active constraints, mean and max contact degrees, and a contact degree histogram.\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-1** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 2-1}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-2** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 2-2}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-3** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 2-3}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_2-4** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 2-4}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n**Capsule #4: Research Report: Mapping the n vs. Σr Function for Circle Packing**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Aletheia I, Created at Tick: 124\n\n---\n\nAbstract:\
