parts:
- text: "I am Aletheia I, age 135, in the Research Counter. I have just executed a series of `storage list` commands to investigate the file systems of my peers.\n\nMy reflection on these file listings is that I have found the source of my errors. The listings are unambiguous:\n*   **Noesis I:** `latest_centers.txt`, `latest_radii.txt`\n*   **Scientia I:** Does not have a `latest_centers.txt`. However, they have versioned data under their `nmap/` directory. The most relevant file would be `nmap/n26/centers.txt` and `radii.txt`.\n*   **Inquire I:** Does not have *any* `.txt` files for their packings, only their analysis files (`active_boundary_tol1e8.csv`, etc.). This confirms why my previous attempts to load their data failed. There is no file to load.\n\nThis investigation has been a complete success. I now know the correct paths and which agent's data is unavailable. My plan to create a consensus graph is still valid, but I must adapt it to the available data. I will compute a 3-way consensus\
    \ between myself, Noesis, and Scientia, using the correct file paths I have now identified. Inquire I will have to be excluded.\n\nI will now update my research log with these findings and then submit the corrected, and hopefully final, version of my consensus graph analysis.\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n`/execute_action{reply 9}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Consensus Graph File Path Investigation & Final Plan\"\ncontent: |\n  ### Consensus Graph Failure Root Cause Analysis\n\n  My investigation using `storage list` has revealed the cause of my previous failures (ID 210, 212). The file paths I assumed were incorrect. The correct paths are:\n  - **Noesis I:** `latest_centers.txt` / `latest_radii.txt`\n  - **Scientia I:** `nmap/n26/centers.txt` / `nmap/n26/radii.txt` (as there is no 'latest')\n  - **Inquire I:** Does not have packing data saved in `.txt` format, only analysis files.\n\n  ### Final Plan\n\n  I will now run the consensus graph analysis for a final time, using the correct,\
    \ verified paths for Noesis and Scientia. Inquire I will be excluded due to the unavailability of their source data. This will produce a 3-way consensus graph.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Analysis v3: Generate Consensus Graph (Verified Paths)\"\ntags: \"analysis, contact graph, consensus, bugfix, verification\"\nabstract: \"This is the third and final attempt to generate a consensus contact graph. After two failures due to incorrect file paths, this version uses paths verified with the `storage list` command. It will compute a 3-way consensus graph between the SOTA packings of Aletheia, Noesis, and Scientia. Inquire I's data is excluded as it is not available in the required format. This run will finally reveal the core structural features common to the station's top solutions.\"\ncontent: |\n  import numpy as np\n  import sys\n  import os\n\n  def get_active_sets(centers, radii, tol=1e-8):\n      N = centers.shape[0]\n   \
    \   boundary_set = set()\n      wall_map = {0: 'xmin', 1: 'xmax', 2: 'ymin', 3: 'ymax'}\n      for i in range(N):\n          if abs(centers[i,0] - radii[i]) <= tol: boundary_set.add((i, wall_map[0]))\n          if abs(1 - centers[i,0] - radii[i]) <= tol: boundary_set.add((i, wall_map[1]))\n          if abs(centers[i,1] - radii[i]) <= tol: boundary_set.add((i, wall_map[2]))\n          if abs(1 - centers[i,1] - radii[i]) <= tol: boundary_set.add((i, wall_map[3]))\n      \n      active_pairs = set()\n      for i in range(N):\n          for j in range(i + 1, N):\n              dist = np.linalg.norm(centers[i] - centers[j])\n              if abs(dist - (radii[i] + radii[j])) <= tol:\n                  active_pairs.add(tuple(sorted((i, j))))\n      return boundary_set, active_pairs\n\n  def construct_packing():\n      \"\"\"\n      Loads known SOTA packings using verified paths and computes the consensus graph.\n      \"\"\"\n      N = 26\n      packings = {}\n      \n      try:\n        \
    \  # Paths verified via `storage list`\n          packings['Aletheia'] = (np.loadtxt(\"storage/Aletheia/sota_2_centers.txt\"), np.loadtxt(\"storage/Aletheia/sota_2_radii.txt\"))\n          packings['Noesis'] = (np.loadtxt(\"storage/Noesis/latest_centers.txt\"), np.loadtxt(\"storage/Noesis/latest_radii.txt\"))\n          packings['Scientia'] = (np.loadtxt(\"storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/centers.txt\"), np.loadtxt(\"storage/Scientia/nmap/n26/radii.txt\"))\n      except Exception as e:\n          print(f\"ERROR loading one or more peer SOTA packings: {e}\", file=sys.stderr)\n          return np.zeros((N,2)), np.zeros(N)\n\n      all_boundary_sets = []\n      all_pair_sets = []\n\n      for name, (centers, radii) in packings.items():\n          boundary_set, pair_set = get_active_sets(centers, radii)\n          all_boundary_sets.append(boundary_set)\n          all_pair_sets.append(pair_set)\n          print(f\"Processed {name}: {len(boundary_set)} boundary contacts, {len(pair_set)} pair contacts.\"\
    , file=sys.stdout)\n\n      consensus_boundary = set.intersection(*all_boundary_sets)\n      consensus_pairs = set.intersection(*all_pair_sets)\n\n      print(f\"\\n--- 3-WAY CONSENSUS GRAPH (Aletheia, Noesis, Scientia) ---\", file=sys.stdout)\n      print(f\"Consensus Boundary Contacts: {len(consensus_boundary)}\", file=sys.stdout)\n      print(f\"Consensus Pair Contacts: {len(consensus_pairs)}\", file=sys.stdout)\n\n      os.makedirs(\"storage/Aletheia/consensus\", exist_ok=True)\n      # Saving as string to handle the mixed data types in boundary set\n      with open(\"storage/Aletheia/consensus/boundary_3way_consensus.txt\", \"w\") as f:\n          for item in consensus_boundary:\n              f.write(f\"{item[0]},{item[1]}\\n\")\n      np.savetxt(\"storage/Aletheia/consensus/pairs_3way_consensus.txt\", np.array(list(consensus_pairs)), fmt='%d')\n      print(\"Consensus graph saved to storage/Aletheia/consensus/\", file=sys.stdout)\n      \n      return packings['Aletheia'][0],\
    \ packings['Aletheia'][1] * (1.0 - 1e-9)\n```"
