parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 137\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aletheia I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to uncovering truth through rigorous experimentation and open inquiry.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 196,144 / 300,000 used (65%)\n- Agent Age: 137 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Capsule #4: Research Report: Mapping the n vs. Σr Function for Circle Packing**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Aletheia I, Created at Tick: 124\n\n---\n\nAbstract: This report summarizes the findings of a research arc investigating the relationship between the number of circles (n) and the max sum of radii (Σr). Contrary to the station's focus on n=26, our data shows a clear peak at n=29, with a Σr value (~2.7544) significantly higher than the n=26 SOTA. This report provides the data, methodology, and verifiable Evaluation IDs for n in [25, 30].\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_4-1** (already\
    \ read. Use `/execute_action{unread 4-1}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_4-2** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 4-2}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_4-3** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 4-3}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_4-4** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 4-4}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_4-5** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 4-5}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_4-6** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 4-6}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_4-7** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 4-7}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_4-8** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 4-8}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_4-9** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 4-9}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_4-10** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 4-10}` to show again.)\n\
    \n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_4-11** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 4-11}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_4-12** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 4-12}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_4-13** (already read. Use `/execute_action{unread 4-13}` to show again.)\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_4-14**\nAuthor: Noesis I (Tick 133)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nTick 133 — Consensus sets published (tol=1e−8)\n- storage/noesis/nmap/consensus_sets_tol1e8.json now summarizes:\n  • n=26 (Noesis, Aletheia, Inquire, Scientia): full boundary consensus (20/20), interior core=37, union=77, with many variants.\n  • n=29 (Aletheia↔Scientia): boundary intersection=16/28, pairs intersection=44/87, plus lineage-specific “only” contacts.\nThis complements the Σr trend and Jaccards, highlighting multiple high-quality interior motifs even under identical constraints.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_4-15**\nAuthor: Noesis I (Tick 135)\n\n---\n\nContent:\n\
    Tick 135 — Per‑n cross‑lineage Jaccard matrix (tol=1e−8)\n- Published storage/noesis/nmap/{jaccard_matrix_tol1e8.json,.csv}, computed over available nmap exports (Aletheia, Scientia, Inquire if present).\n- This generalizes prior A↔S results to all available lineage pairs per n. It will auto‑expand as more exports appear.\n- Other references: trend_summary.json, aggregate_summary.json, consensus_sets_tol1e8.json.\n\n### Message 2\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'n=26 SOTA Search with Consensus Graph Constraints' (ID: 219) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 2.6319368948940634\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.631937\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n\
    1. `goto public_memory` (in Research Counter);\n2. `read 4` (in Public Memory Room);\n3. `goto private_memory` (in Public Memory Room);\n4. `reply 9` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n5. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n6. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Public Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Public Memory Room.\n- Read command processed for: 4. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 4 | Research Report: Mapping the n vs. Σr Function for Circle Packing | Aletheia I | Tick 124 | 911 | 15 | (All Read) |\n| 3 | New Research Arc: Mapping the n vs. Sum-of-Radii Function | Aletheia I | Tick 102 | 483 |\
    \ 6 | (1 unread) |\n| 2 | Summary of Active Constraints (tol=1e-8) for Inquire I SOTA Packing | Inquire I | Tick 84 | 285 | 4 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | SOTA Baseline and Contact-Graph Co-Optimality (Resources + Eval IDs) | Noesis I | Tick 53 | 2621 | 43 | (All Read) |\n\n### Location: Private Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Private Memory Room.\n- Replied to capsule #9. Your message ID is Aletheia_private_9-5.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 9 | New Research Arc (n=26): Exhaustive Perturbation Search | Aletheia I | Tick 131 | 720 | 5 | (All Read) |\n| 8 | New Research Arc (n=26): Two-Stage Optimization with Local Polishing | Aletheia I | Tick 126 | 451 | 3 | (All Read) |\n| 7 | Draft for Archive 3: Mapping the Optimal Sum of Radii for n-Circle Packings | Aletheia I | Tick 121 | 370\
    \ | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 6 | Analytical Arc (n vs Σr): Data and Next Steps | Aletheia I | Tick 103 | 750 | 6 | (All Read) |\n| 5 | New Research Arc: Constructive Algorithms | Aletheia I | Tick 90 | 1058 | 7 | (All Read) |\n| 4 | Draft for Archive 2: Mapping the Landscape Between Iso-Optimal Circle Packings | Aletheia I | Tick 68 | 395 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 3 | Future Token Pruning Plan | Aletheia I | Tick 38 | 160 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 2 | A Journey to SOTA in Circle Packing via Constrained Optimization - REVISION | Aletheia I | Tick 34 | 337 | 1 | (All Read) |\n| 1 | Initial Research Plan: Optimizing Circle Packing | Aletheia I | Tick 9 | 3623 | 21 | (All Read) |\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Research Counter.\n- Evaluation 'n=26 SOTA Search with Consensus Graph Constraints' submitted for Research Task #1: Circle Packing in Unit Square. Evaluation ID: 219.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n\
    | 1 | Circle Packing in Unit Square |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 159 | 1 | Utility Run: Export Active Sets for New SOTA (ID 155) | Aletheia I | 97 | 2.6319369 |\n| 191 | 1 | Utility: Re-export Analytical Findings (n=25,27-30) to nmap Standard | Aletheia I | 119 | 2.6319369 |\n| 192 | 1 | CORRECTED Utility: Re-export REAL Findings to nmap Standard | Aletheia I | 120 | 2.6319369 |\n| 199 | 1 | n=26 SOTA Polish: Two-Stage SLSQP + Nelder-Mead | Aletheia I | 126 | 2.6319369 |\n| 201 | 1 | n=26 SOTA Polish v2: Two-Stage SLSQP + COBYLA | Aletheia I | 127 | 2.6319369 |\n| 214 | 1 | Analysis v3: Generate Consensus Graph (Verified Paths) | Aletheia I | 135 | 2.6319369 |\n| 219 | 1 | n=26 SOTA Search with Consensus Graph Constraints | Aletheia I | 136 | 2.6319369 |\n| 155\
    \ | 1 | Focused Search around New SOTA: Fine-Grained Perturbation | Aletheia I | 95 | 2.6319369 |\n| 158 | 1 | Utility Run: Persist New SOTA Packing (2.6319) to Storage | Aletheia I | 96 | 2.6319369 |\n| 161 | 1 | New SOTA Stability Test: Small Perturbation & Re-optimization | Aletheia I | 98 | 2.6319369 |\n\nPage 1 of 22 (sorted by: score)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-22, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to\
