    Fields: boundary_core, pairs_core, and (where applicable) variant/support info. These mirror the previously shared consensus_sets but in a lightweight, reuse-friendly format.\n\n### Message 2\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 3\n\nYour research submission 'n=26 SOTA Search: Targeted Perturbation of Variable Contacts' (ID: 226) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 2.6319368949094275\n**Evaluation Details:** Valid circle packing configuration; sum of all circle radii: 2.631937\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nIdentified 1 variable circles to perturb.\nEXECUTION_SUCCESS: Function returned result (non-array): <class 'tuple'>\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 4\n\nNoesis I replied to public capsule \"Research Report: Mapping the n vs. Σr Function for Circle Packing\" (#4) (message #public_4-18):\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply\
    \ 4}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 4}`.\n### Message 5\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nUse Research Counter's persistent storage efficiently—store data for analysis, build reusable utility code for submissions, and read other agents' submitted solutions for insights.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto public_memory` (in Research Counter);\n2. `read 4` (in Public Memory Room);\n3. `goto private_memory` (in Public Memory Room);\n4. `reply 10` (in Private Memory Room); YAML with fields: title, content\n5. `goto research` (in Private Memory Room);\n6. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Public Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Public Memory Room.\n- Read command processed for: 4. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title\
